\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Peso weak, others hold ground despite yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 678 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2005\par 09:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Feb 21 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  shrugged off\par the weakness in the Japanese yen on Monday and held their\par ground, despite the increasing threat of regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Philippine peso was among the only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken\par notably, because of worries that legislators might reject or\par water down a proposed system of value-added tax. The peso fell\par to 54.85 per dollar from opening levels around 54.70.\par     The Korean won, Taiwan dollar and Singapore dollar\par maintained narrow ranges even as the yen shed nearly half a\par percent from Friday, driven lower by last week's weak Japanese\par economic data and waning expectations of any immediate change\par in China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime.\par  \par     That led the yen-won cross rate to weaken to around 9.67\par won per yen, close to two-year lows struck in overnight deals.\par     "We think Korea has delinked from yen, as has the rest of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia," said one Singapore-based trader. "And, now the problem  \f28 \par \par \uc2 is that the market has been caught long yen/won and is  \par \par \uc2 scrambling to sell."  \par \par \uc2 Traders believe the South Korean authorities target the  \par \par \uc2 won's level against the yen, since the two countries export  \par \par \uc2 similar products. But for almost a month the yen has stayed  \par \par \uc2 below 10 won, the level that analysts believe is the lowest  \par \par \uc2 South Korea is comfortable with.  \par \par \uc2 The won rose to near 1,022 a dollar on Monday, within  \par \par \uc2 striking distance of last week's seven-year peak, as Korean  \par \par \uc2 stocks hit a five-year high on news a fund had invested $975  \par \par \uc2 million in Korean conglomerate LG Corp. and its unit.  \par \par \uc2 Won bulls shrugged off news of further issuance of bonds by  \par \par \uc2 the Bank of Korea, to absorb the won funds released during  \par \par \uc2 dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WORRY  \par \par \uc2 Still, the worry of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 markets in India, Taiwan, \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Korea. Thailand's and  \par \par \uc2 India's reserves data showed heavy dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar was held back from four-year highs beyond  \par \par \uc2 31.50 by talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to cap  \par \par \uc2 the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign portfolio investment inflows are putting upward  \par \par \uc2 pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Foreigners have bought close to T$100  \par \par \uc2 billion of Taiwan shares since late January and the market hit  \par \par \uc2 its highest in nine months on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht was in a range of 38.53 to 38.60 per dollar,  \par \par \uc2 while the Sing dollar was on the firmer side of 1.64 per  \par \par \uc2 dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said Thailand had received over $1 billion of  \par \par \uc2 foreign portfolio investments so far in 2005, more than in any  \par \par \uc2 year from 2001 to 2004.  \par \par \uc2 "The big theme at the moment is whether or not dollar  \par \par \uc2 weakness is going to resume," said John Cairns, head of  \par \par \uc2 research at IDEAglobal.com.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The more the dollar stays here, the more people are going\par to be worried about their long Asia positions," he said.\par     The moves in Hong Kong forwards and Taiwan dollar\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 non-deliverable forwards also confirmed speculators were  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trimming their Asian positions, he added.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day at 0809 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.69         105.24       -0.43\par  Sing dlr        1.6379         1.6391       +0.07\par  Taiwan dlr      31.516         31.520       +0.01\par  Korean won     1023.10        1024.00       +0.09\par  Baht             38.58          38.57       -0.01\par  Peso             54.88          54.70       -0.34\par  Rupiah         9272.00        9255.00       -0.18\par  Rupee            43.79          43.83       +0.10\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.69         102.45       -3.07\par  Sing dlr        1.6379         1.6310       -0.42\par  Taiwan dlr      31.516         31.917       +1.27\par  Korean won     1023.10        1035.10       +1.17\par  Baht             38.58          38.85       +0.71\par  Peso             54.88          56.28       +2.55\par  Rupiah         9272.00        9270.00       -0.02\par  Rupee            43.79          43.47       -0.72.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050221e12l007kg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*