\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won at 7-year high on share purchases.  \b0\par\par\uc2 780 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2005\par 09:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 19 (Reuters) - The South Korean won rose to\par a fresh seven-year high on Wednesday, boosted by foreign\par purchases of stocks, and leading Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher as the\par G7 presses Asian central banks to allow their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par appreciate.\par     The won, Asia's best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2004,\par strengthened half a percent to 1,030.2 per dollar, a level\par where traders said state-owned banks probably \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par buying dollars to help keep exports competitive.\par     Foreign investors were net sellers of about 21 billion won\par in Korean stocks on Wednesday, but had bought a net 623 billion\par won worth of shares in the previous three sessions.\par     "There's equity-related buying on behalf of foreign\par investors," said Sani Hamid, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at 4CAST Ltd.\par in Singapore.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  "Then there's the G7 calling for stronger Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     China was likely to come under pressure from the Group of\par Seven nations at a meeting in February to loosen its control on\par the yuan and allow the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to appreciate, analysts said. A\par stronger yuan would boost other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The baht matched its 4-1/2-year high of 38.38 per dollar\par with further gains held back by suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy dollars. The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left its key\par 14-day repo rate unchanged at 2.0 percent, as expected.\par     The Taiwan dollar and the Philippine peso each gained a\par third of a percent and the Singapore dollar strengthened a\par fifth of a percent.\par     "Everyone wants to hold a bullish position on Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in case China does move," said Mark Cranfield, head\par of treasury at Landesbank Baden-Wuerttemberg in Singapore.\par  \par     "Personally, I think they won't. It's too early. China\par wants to fix its banking system first."\par     The premiums on one-month, three-month and six-month yuan\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 non-deliverable forwards - agreements that investors use to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bet on any change in the yuan's value in the future - have  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 been pared back after surging through the fourth quarter of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2004.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. DEFICIT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held their ground even after data on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tuesday alleviated concerns that the United States was unable  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to attract enough foreign capital to fund its record trade  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 deficit. Those concerns were responsible for the dollar's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 decline last year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign investors pumped $81 billion into U.S. assets in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November, hitting a five-month high and exceeding average  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 forecasts of $55 billion. The surge in inflows more than  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 covered a record $60.3 billion U.S. trade deficit in the same  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 month.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Some analysts cautioned that the inflows were not so\par impressive when compared with the same month last year.\par     Inflows from abroad were $8 billion higher than November\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2003, while the U.S. trade deficit was $21 billion wider than a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 year earlier, Ashley Davies, a strategist at UBS, said in a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 note.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "So while the U.S. funding requirement has increased,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 portfolio investors are only grudgingly opening their wallets,"  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With longer-term concerns about the dollar unchanged, Asian  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are likely to outperform other major world  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the euro and the Australian dollar this  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 year, Standard Chartered Bank said in a report, adding that the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore dollar was its top pick in Asia.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We still think (Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) can appreciate further  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the dollar in the first half and significantly against  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the euro in the second half given the strong balance of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 payments, tsunami-related aid, infrastructure spending and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 euro-overvaluation," the bank said. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day at 0800 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       102.35         102.63       +0.27\par  Sing dlr     