\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Ascent slows as yen, won stall.  \b0\par\par\uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2004\par 04:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 24 (Reuters) - A rally in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par against a broadly weaker U.S. dollar slowed on Wednesday as the\par threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reined in the Korean won and Japanese\par yen.\par     The dollar fell to record lows past $1.31 against the euro\par   overnight and plumbed new lows versus other European\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     But it held its ground against the yen        as the\par Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  found it hard to scale an April 2000 peak\par near 102.75 per dollar struck last week.\par     The Korean won                   was quoted around 1,065 a\par dollar, having come off a 7-year high of 1,060 on successive\par sessions this week after state-run banks were seen buying\par dollars aggressively.\par  \par     The Taiwan dollar          hit a high of 32.41 but was\par still some distance away from Friday's 3-=   year peak.\par     However, Reuters data showed the Singapore dollar\par rose to 1.6433, a new 6-year high, and the Thai baht  was\par quoted at 39.74, its highest since May.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I don't think anyone is fighting the (weak dollar) trend,"\par said Philip Wee, strategist with DBS Bank.\par     "The won has outdone even the yen and is too strong\par relative to the region. The Koreans have a case for smoothening\par the won's move."\par     The won has risen nearly 5 percent this month, compared\par with the yen's 2 percent, the Taiwan dollar's 3 percent and the\par Singapore dollar's 1 percent gains.\par     Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said on Wednesday\par the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stall the rising\par baht.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        and the Philippine peso\par continued as regional laggards, holding steady levels.\par     In Singapore, analysts differed on how much further the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore dollar could rise before it hit the top end of the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 undisclosed trade-weighed band within which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary  \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore guides the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DBS' Wee said his estimates showed the Singapore dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 would hit the top of the band, which he takes as 5 percent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 wide, when it rises to 1.6360.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day at 0234 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.46         103.34       -0.12\par  Sing dlr        1.6430         1.6468       +0.23\par  Taiwan dlr      32.446         32.487       +0.13\par  Korean won     1065.70        1065.70       +0.00\par  Baht             39.75          39.87       +0.30\par  Peso             56.31          56.29       -0.04\par  Rupiah         8990.00        9000.00       +0.11\par  Rupee            45.04          45.04       +0.00\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.46         107.31       +3.72\par  Sing dlr   