\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Ends At Fresh 6.5-Month High; Most Bonds Down  \b0\par\par\uc2 876 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2004\par 11:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended at its highest level in six-and-a-half months in Asian spot trade Monday, as the U.S. unit fell in global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan said U.S. deficits will bring further weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Most Thai government bond prices fell, as Greenspan also promised in comments late Friday to continue raising interest rates. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, limited losses to mostly short- and medium-term bonds.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar finished at THB39.84, down from THB40.21 at the Asian close Friday. The close was its lowest level since May 7, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit crashed through pyschological resistance at THB40.00 during the New York session Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Follow-through selling by big-name investment houses finally pushed the dollar under THB39.90 late in Asian trade Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said volume was very thin, but the Bank of Thailand stood aside Monday to let the baht catch up with the rise of the yen against the dollar late Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Monday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will try to limit volatility and speculative activity which affect the country's trade, but that it can't really \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend.  \par \par \uc2 He said the recent strength of the baht was due to U.S. efforts to weaken the dollar. Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said earlier Monday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is monitoring the situation, but that the baht's strength is due to general dollar weakness, not speculative pressure.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the dollar to trade overnight in a range of THB39.75 to THB39.90. Further weakness is expected in the dollar due to the massive U.S. current account and budget deficits, but traders expect the market to pause for profit taking and to avoid provoking Asian central banks into \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ 22-11-04 1050GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Short- and medium-term government bond yields rose, tracking U.S. Treasury yields higher after Greenspan's comments on interest rates. However, buying by the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in issues due August 2010 and March 2011 limited increases in the long end of the curve, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 They expect yields in the short end of the yield curve to remain under pressure from rising interest rates, likely flattening the yield curve.  \par \par \uc2 Some economists have said they don't believe the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise its 14-day repurchase market target rate from the current 1.75% at its next policy meeting on Dec. 15, due to expectations that economic growth will slow next year.  \par \par \uc2 But if the U.S. federal funds rate rises 25 basis points to 2.25% in mid-December, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be reluctant to let the premium over the Thai policy rate rise to 50 basis points.  \par \par \uc2 The average bid late Monday on the government bond due December 2006 rose six basis points to 2.725%; the December 2008 bid climbed five basis points to 3.613%; the November 2009 bid edged up one basis point to 4.153%; the August 2010 bid was flat at 4.274%; the October 2013 bid was flat at 4.90%; and the August 2019 bid rose one basis point to 5.35%, the Thai Bond Dealing Center said.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Thailand said it auctioned THB5 billion worth of 28-day treasury bills Monday at a weighted-average accepted yield of 1.595%, down from 1.619% at last week's auction, due to demand for paper maturing shortly after next month's interest rate policy meeting. In the secondary market, the average bid yield on 28-day T-bills eased to 1.600% from 1.632% late Friday, the Thai Bond Dealing Center said.  \par \par \uc2 Auction yields on 92- and 182-day T-bills rose, however, due to the rising risk of interest rate increases over the terms.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctioned THB5 billion in 92-day T-bills at an average 1.786%, up from 1.748% last week. The average secondary market bid edged down to 1.773% from 1.774%, however, because many investors want paper that matures early next year.  \par \par \uc2 Five billion baht worth of 182-day T-bills were auctioned at an average 2.239%, up from 2.156% last week. The secondary market bid jumped to 2.255% from 2.167% Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The secondary market bid on 364-day \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds rose to 2.487% from 2.466% Friday, but dealers expect yields above 2.5% in Tuesday's auction, which will also put another THB5 billion of supply in the market.  \par \par \uc2 The most-active overnight interbank rate was likely flat around 1.70%, with banks mostly prepared for the end Monday of a biweekly cash reserve period, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Market     Term            Monday               Friday \par Interbank  Overnight/ \par            Most Active     1.70000% (Estimate)  1.70000% \par Repurchase Overnight/Close 1.68750% (Actual)    1.68750% \par            14-Day          1.75000%             1.75000% \par            1-Month         no activity          no activity \par            3-Month         no activity          no activity \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2266 0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 22-11-04 1110GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1028 1861  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041122e0bm000jc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
