\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Ctrl Bk Chief: Will Try To Mitigate Baht Volatility  \b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2004\par 06:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will try to mitigate the volatility in the baht as an excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement may attract speculation and affect the country's trade, its governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Monday.  \par \par \uc2 However, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't rally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to drive the baht against the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend.  \par \par \uc2 "We will do the best we can to reduce the impact (of baht volatility) on trade. But, we can't really \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We can't go against the market trend," he told reporters. [ 22-11-04 0537GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn said the baht's recent strength is mainly due to efforts by the U.S. to weaken the dollar. Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said early Monday that the baht's strength is due to a general dollar weakness, not speculation.  \par \par \uc2 At 0542, the dollar was quoted at 39.885 baht, a near seven-month low, down from THB39.90 early and THB40.07 at Friday's close in Asian spot trade. The baht has gained around 3% in the past three weeks.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bangkok Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com [ 22-11-04 0603GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041122e0bm00056\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
