\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Thai Baht Ends At Fresh 6.5-Month High; Most Bonds Down  \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2004\par 12:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2004, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended at its highest level in six-and-a-half months in Asian spot trade Monday, as the U.S. unit fell in global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan said U.S. deficits will bring further weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Most Thai government bond prices fell, as Greenspan also promised in comments late Friday to continue raising interest rates. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, limited losses to mostly short- and medium-term bonds.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar finished at THB39.84, down from THB40.21 at the Asian close Friday. The close was its lowest level since May 7, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit crashed through pyschological resistance at THB40.00 during the New York session Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Follow-through selling by big-name investment houses finally pushed the dollar under THB39.90 late in Asian trade Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said volume was very thin, but the Bank of Thailand stood aside Monday to let the baht catch up with the rise of the yen against the dollar late Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Monday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will try to limit volatility and speculative activity which affect the country's trade, but that it can't really \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend.  \par \par \uc2 He said the recent strength of the baht was due to U.S. efforts to weaken the dollar. Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said earlier Monday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is monitoring the situation, but that the baht's strength is due to general dollar weakness, not speculative pressure.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the dollar to trade overnight in a range of THB39.75 to THB39.90. Further weakness is expected in the dollar due to the massive U.S. current account and budget deficits, but traders expect the market to pause for profit taking and to avoid provoking Asian central banks into \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020041122e0bm0063i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
