\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dlr, won hit multi-year highs.  \b0\par\par\uc2 749 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2004\par 10:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 18 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar rallied\par to a 6-year high against the dollar and the South Korean won\par hit a new 7-year high on Thursday as worries about the U.S.\par current account deficit saw the dollar sold against most\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Analysts said attention was focused on this weekend's\par meeting in Germany of finance officials from the Group of 20\par developed and developing nations, which could provide clues as\par to whether Asian governments would tolerate further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strength.\par     The Singapore dollar        traded as high as 1.6448 per\par dollar, its strongest level since December 1998. It could\par strengthen further because the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\par has a tightening bias for monetary policy, Bank of America\par strategist Simon Flint said.\par     The won        surged 1.5 percent to a high of 1,063.8 per\par dollar, a high since November 1997.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has gained 7.5\par percent since the start of October and 12 percent this year,\par making it Asia's best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the dollar.\par  \par     The dollar fell to a record low against the euro        and\par was at seven-and-a-half month lows against the yen on Thursday.\par     "If the (G20) meeting comes out with no clear conclusions,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 then chances are that the market could go for a sell-dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 mode again," said Christy Tan, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at 4CAST Ltd.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in Singapore.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "We do see some outperformance by the Taiwan dollar and the\par Sing dollar in the next few weeks."\par     The Taiwan dollar          gained 0.8 percent to a new\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 three-and-half year high, helped by the broader dollar weakness  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and optimism about domestic economic growth that has driven  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's benchmark stock index 6 percent higher this month.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  and the Indian rupee          are\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 other possible gainers among Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the coming  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 weeks, provided that their central banks do not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Tan  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thursday that short-term foreign funds inflows had risen this  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 week, but not to a worrying level that would require the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to step in.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The baht strengthened to 40.04 per dollar. The rupee was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 little changed at 45.04 per dollar on worries about  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian central banks \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily from 2002 to early  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2004 to limit \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains against a weakening dollar,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 building up reserve holdings of more than $2.2 trillion as they  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 sought to protect their export sectors.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But Asian investors and exporters have sold the dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 since October on concern about the U.S. budget and trade  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 deficits, and an expectation that Asian central banks would let  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthen to help check inflation.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Traders and investors will also watch the G20 meeting for\par signals from China about a yuan revaluation, Tan said.\par     European and U.S. officials have said China should let its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthen because the peg of 8.28 per dollar unfairly\par benefits Chinese exporters.\par     Flint expects China to let the yuan appreciate by the end\par of the first quarter of 2005.\par     European officials at the G20 could also bring pressure to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bear on counterparts from China, South Korea and Japan -  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 countries that have a high trade surpluses with the U.S. - to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 let their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthen further given the euro was at  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 record highs, Flint said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0805 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.76         104.99       +1.19\par  Sing dlr        1.6447         1.6490       +0.26\par  Taiwan dlr      32.410         32.659       +0.77\par  Korean won     1065.40        1081.20       +1.48\par  Baht             40.04          40.20       +0.40\par  Peso             56.29          56.36       +0.12\par  Rupee            45.04          45.03       -0.01\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.76         107.31       +3.42\par  Sing dlr        1.6447         1.6978       +3.23\par  Taiwan dlr      32.410         33.978       +4.84\par  Korean won     1065.40        1192.00      +11.88\par  Baht             40.04          39.59       -1.14\par  Peso             56.29          55.49       -1.42\par  Rupiah         8992.00        8410.00       -6.47\par  Rupee            45.04          45.60       +1.24 ((Editing by\par John Mair; rajat.bhattacharya@reuters.com; Reuters Messaging:\par rajat.bhattacharya.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870 3841))\par     For the new Reuters scrolling global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  service please\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 click .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041118e0bi007ce\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
