\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Thai c.bank not to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  on baht.   \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 2004\par 07:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Nov 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made it clear on Monday it was comfortable with the baht's recent gains against the dollar and has no plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow its advance.   \par \par \uc2 The baht traded at around 40.29/32 per dollar at midday Monday, against 41.04 at the close on November 1.   \par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula told reporters he believed the baht was at an appropriate level as it had moved mostly in line with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The baht had not gained against yen or euro, he said.   \par \par \uc2 "We don't have to do anything. Ours is at the right level. We should not look just at its exchange rate against the dollar, but should compare it with yen and euro," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Thai exports remained competitive despite the baht's recent steady gains, Pridiyathorn said.   \par \par \uc2 "The baht is still competitive when compared with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because its real effective exchange rate has moved in the same direction as other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Thai exports rose a robust 25.4 percent during the third quarter against the same period of 2003, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said financial markets appeared to have adjusted slowly to lingering security problems in Thailand's Muslim south since 85 Muslims died at a public protest and in military custody on October 25.   \par \par \uc2 "Investors said that although sentiment has not turned clearly positive, people are getting used to the current bad news regarding the violence in the South," said research house 4Cast in Singapore.   \par \par \uc2 "With confidence gradually re-emerging, foreigners are buying Thai assets again and the downward USD trend intact, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators are building up their short USD/THB positions.   \par \par \uc2 "Going forward, we expect USD/THB to hover around 40.30-40 early week before drifting south again in line with softer USD/Asia tone," 4Cast said in a note to clients.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041115e0bf004n1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
