\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won retreats amid focus on policy.  \b0\par\par\uc2 700 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2004\par 09:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 10 (Reuters) - The Korean won retreated from\par seven-year highs on Wednesday, ahead of rate decisions in the\par United States and South Korea, as markets renewed their debate\par about Seoul's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy.\par     The won fell to 1,110 a dollar, dropping from a seven-year\par peak overnight of 1,102, the highest since the Asian financial\par crisis in 1997.\par     Traders reported dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Korean\par authorities and that, coming just a day before a rate-setting\par meeting, sparked a debate about policy intentions.\par     Some analysts said Korean authorities would not let the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rise past 1,100 a dollar, a level they have in the\par past said affects the profitability of smaller exporters.\par Besides, the won has outperformed the region by rallying seven\par percent this year and would now pause, analysts said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The head of the Bank of Korea's international department\par Rhee Gwang-ju told Reuters on Wednesday sentiment in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market had substantially tilted to one side\par recently.\par  \par    Rhee said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was watching the won's moves and\par was prepared to act to balance market sentiment if necessary.\par     "Many in the market are speculating that the BoK has agreed\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to cut rates in exchange for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economics (MOFE) allowing further won strength. As such a rate  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 cut would further damage perception of BoK independence from  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the government," economists at UBS said in a note to clients.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     A Reuters poll showed most economists expect the Bank of\par Korea to hold rates steady at record lows on Thursday.\par     UBS said many market participants were speculating that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will cut rates.\par     "This would confirm in their minds that the policy mix has\par been shifted in favour of the domestic sector at the expense of\par export competitiveness," UBS said.\par     If rates were kept unchanged, the won could fall, UBS said.\par     RUPIAH WEAKER\par     The Indonesian rupiah fell over half a percent as markets\par covered positions ahead of holidays.\par     Indonesian markets are closed next week for a Muslim\par festival. Several centres in the region are shut on Thursday\par and Monday for festival holidays.\par     "There is some covering of short dollar positions,\par especially the shorter term and interbank names," said David\par Simmonds, markets strategist with the Royal Bank of Scotland.\par     "Also, there has definitely been more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  talk\par around in Korea, perhaps in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and probably some stepped\par up physical \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  too," he said.\par     Simmonds said the dollar-buying by regional authorities\par seemed aimed at smoothing the appreciation of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rather than thwarting the trend.\par     The U.S. dollar was slightly higher against the euro and\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 yen after European officials warned markets about the euro's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rise and ahead of a U.S. Federal Reserve decision on rates. A  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quarter point rise in U.S. rates is widely expected and priced  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore dollar fell a quarter cent to 1.6550/60 a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar. The Taiwan dollar shed about 0.4 percent, hitting 33.11  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a dollar and descending from Tuesday's seven-month high of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 32.85.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai baht was off an overnight five-month high of 40.52  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a dollar and was quoted around 40.70/75.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day at 0820 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.02         105.68       -0.32\par  Sing dlr        1.6556         1.6522       -0.21\par  Taiwan dlr      33.117         32.974       -0.43\par  Korean won     1110.30        1103.50       -0.61\par  Baht             40.73          40.69       -0.10\par  Peso             56.34          56.28       -0.11\par  Rupiah         9036.00        8981.00       -0.61\par  Rupee            45.14          45.15       +0.03\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.02         107.31       +1.22\par  Sing dlr        1.6556         1.6978       +2.55\par  Taiwan dlr      33.117         33.978       +2.60\par  Korean won     1110.30        1192.00       +7.36\par  Baht             40.73          39.59       -2.81\par  Peso             56.34          55.49       -1.51\par  Rupiah         9036.00        8410.00       -6.93\par  Rupee          