\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Down on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk.  \b0\par\par\uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2004\par 04:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 10 (Reuters) - The Korean won and Indonesian\par rupiah led declines in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday amid talk\par of dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and ahead of several upcoming\par regional holidays.\par     The U.S. dollar was slightly higher against the euro\par and yen  after European officials echoed European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central\par Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Jean-Claude Trichet's concerns on the rising euro and\par ahead of a U.S. Federal Reserve decision on rates due later in\par the day. A quarter point rise in U.S. rates is widely expected\par and priced in.\par     The won                   fell to 1,108 per dollar in\par morning trading, off a seven-year peak of 1,102 overnight. That\par level was the won's highest following the end of the Asian\par financial crisis.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The head of the Bank of Korea's international department\par Rhee Gwang-ju told Reuters on Wednesday sentiment in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market had substantially tilted recently and\par that the dollar's decline against the won wasn't small compared\par with other major world \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \par     Rhee said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was watching the won's moves and\par was prepared to act if needed to address the imbalance.\par     The Singapore dollar        was barely changed around\par 1.6530/40 a dollar while the Indonesian rupiah fell over half a\par percent as markets covered positions ahead of holidays.\par     Indonesian markets are closed next week for a Muslim\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 festival. Several regional markets will be closed on Thursday  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for the Hindu festival of lights and on Monday to mark the end  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of the Muslim fasting month of Ramadan.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There is some covering of short dollar positions,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 especially the shorter term and interbank names," said David  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Simmonds, markets strategist with the Royal Bank of Scotland.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Also, there has definitely been more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  talk  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 around in Korea, perhaps in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and probably some stepped  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 up physical \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  too," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Simmonds said the dollar-buying by regional authorities  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 seemed aimed at smoothing the appreciation of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 rather than thwarting the trend.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Traders suspected the Taiwan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was partly\par responsible for the stalling and retracement of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Taiwan dollar          had risen about 1.8 percent this\par month, hitting a seven-month high of 32.85 on Tuesday. It was\par back below 33 on Wednesday.\par     The Thai baht        was off an overnight five-month high\par of 40.52 a dollar, and quoted around 40.64/66.\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  Change on the day at   0255 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.78         105.68       -0.09\par  Sing dlr        1.6531         1.6522       -0.05\par  Taiwan dlr      32.995         32.974       -0.06\par  Korean won     1108.00        1103.50       -0.41\par  Baht             40.64          40.69       +0.12\par  Peso             56.30          56.28       -0.04\par  Rupiah         9043.00        8981.00       -0.69\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.78         107.31       +1.45\par  Sing dlr        1.6531         1.6978       +2.70\par  Taiwan dlr      32.995         33.978       +2.98\par  Korean won     1108.00        1192.00       +7.58\par  Baht             40.64          39.59       -2.60\par  Peso             56.30          55.49       -1.44\par  Rupiah         9043.00        8410.00       -7.00\par  Rupee            45.15          45.60       +0.99.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041110e0ba002xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
