\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Southeast Asians feel pressure.  \b0\par\par\uc2 754 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2004\par 11:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     SINGAPORE, Aug 30 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were pulled\par down as the Japanese yen weakened past 110 per dollar on\par Monday, with Southeast Asia leading the losses.\par     The Philippine peso has been hobbled by government talk of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  a fiscal crisis, markets are cautious on the Indonesian rupiah   \par \par \uc2  ahead of next month's presidential vote, and a slowing economy   \par \par \uc2  and persistent violence in Thailand's south have pushed the   \par \par \uc2  baht to one-year lows.   \par \par \uc2  "There's definitely a strongish dollar trend which is going   \par \par \uc2  through, underlying all of this," Bank of America strategist   \par \par \uc2  Sameer Goel said, pointing to the dollar's gains against the   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     In north Asia, a return of foreign investors to equity\par markets, notably Taiwan, and easing oil prices offered support.\par     Oil prices were steady above $43 a barrel, and dealers\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected more retracement from record highs, while stock\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets were flat to softer but holding onto their gains of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent weeks.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah softened beyond 9,360 per dollar, its\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weakest since just before the first round of presidential\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par elections in early July.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In recent weeks, the market had been capped by a wariness\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around 9,300 per dollar, although\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par traders said the bank was not a buyer on Monday as the rupiah's\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fall was not drastic.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah has lost more than 10 percent against the U.S.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar this year and is expected to stay under pressure ahead\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the September 20 presidential vote pitting incumbent\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Megawati Sukarnoputri against market favourite Susilo Bambang\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Yudhoyono.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso extended last week's slide to hit a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par two-month low of 56.25 per dollar. The peso has been under\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressure since President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo said last week\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that the country was suffering a fiscal crisis.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Goel said Arroyo's words seemed aimed at putting the need\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for fiscal reform on the domestic political agenda to gain\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support for her plans to bring the budget deficit under\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par control.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There is a risk involved in using strong words like\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 'fiscal crisis' which obviously gets people rather worried, but\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par I still do feel there is no indication therein that they are\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par actually thinking about reneging on their debt or any such\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par drastic steps," he said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Data showing Philippine GDP had risen by a stronger than\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected 6.2 percent in the year through the second quarter\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offered the peso little respite.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht held near last week's one-year low, but the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market was wary of the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if it\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weakened past 41.70 per dollar.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai Finance Ministry trimmed its 2004 growth forecast\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 6.5 to 7.0 percent, from 7.1 percent, due to higher oil\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prices and slower growth in the first quarter.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN FLOWS\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar opened local trade testing resistance at\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 34.00 per dollar, a level that has held since late July.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, its early strength soon disappeared and it retreated\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par past Friday's local close.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Similarly, the Korean won hit a peak of 1,150 per dollar,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its highest since July 14, but then gradually weakened with the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen to end slightly softer.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Goel said that in the last two weeks' foreign equity flows\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to Taiwan had picked up for the first time since the disputed\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par presidential election in March, although he cautioned it was\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par too soon to say if it was a sustained trend.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "In trade-weighted terms, the Taiwan dollar has been pretty\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weak in the last few months, and I do feel that that trend\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could turn around if the flows were to continue to come back,"\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par he said.\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       110.09         109.45       -0.58\par  Sing dlr        1.7147         1.7107       -0.23\par  Taiwan dlr      34.079         34.065       -0.04\par  Korean won     1154.50        1153.00       -0.13\par  Baht             41.65          41.59       -0.14\par  Peso             56.21          56.15       -0.11\par  Rupiah         9335.00        9295.00       -0.43\par  Rupee            46.36          46.32       -0.08\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       110.09         107.31       -2.53\par  Sing dlr        1.7147         1.6978       -0.99\par  Taiwan dlr      34.079         33.978       -0.30\par  Korean won     1154.50        1192.00       +3.25\par  Baht             41.65          39.59       -4.96\par  Peso             56.21          55.49       -1.28\par  Rupiah         9335.00        8410.00       -9.91\par  Rupee            46.36          45.60       -1.64.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040830e08u0080z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
