\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Ctrl Bk Denies  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Says Econ Resilient  \b0\par\par\uc2 740 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2004\par 12:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday rejected market speculation that it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the baht after last week's U.S. interest rate hike triggered talk of capital flows out of Thailand.  \par \par \uc2 The bank also said the Thai economy continues to be robust despite rising oil prices and, now, yet another outbreak of bird flu.  \par \par \uc2 Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after the Federal Reserve hiked its federal-funds rate by 25 basis points, since capital flows and the baht have been stable.  \par \par \uc2 "We haven't done anything. Things have been stable for quite some time," Pridiyathorn told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Open Market Committee lifted its federal-funds target rate to 1.25% from a 46-year low of 1.00%, putting it on par with Thailand's 14-day repurchase market target rate.  \par \par \uc2 The Fed action hasn't had any impact on local financial markets as the move was in line with market expectations and was already priced in, Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 Many economists are now saying the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely wait until the U.S. raises the federal-funds target by another 25 basis points before making a similar move to keep its 14-day rate on a similar footing.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, Pridiyathorn said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Committee will provide clear signals about its expectations for interest rate policy in the months ahead after its upcoming meeting on July 21.  \par \par \uc2 He left open the possibility of leaving the 14-day rate unchanged at the meeting, with local financial system liquidity high and core inflation still low.  \par \par \uc2 Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Still Bullish On Economy  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn said he isn't overly concerned about the state of the Thai economy which has showed resilience against negative factors such as high oil prices and a fresh bird flu outbreak.  \par \par \uc2 Higher oil prices haven't significantly pushed up inflation, with most consumer products produced locally.  \par \par \uc2 The June CPI rose 0.2% from May and 3% over the year-ago month. Core inflation, which excludes volatile energy and fresh food prices, was up 0.5% on year and flat on month.  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn said Thailand's high foreign reserves, currently around $43 billion, and an expected current account surplus, will act as a cushion against any external shocks.  \par \par \uc2 Even though higher oil prices may push the country's trade balance into the red this year, the current account balance is expected to remain in surplus at least until 2006, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn earlier forecast that this year's trade balance could range from a deficit of as much as $500 million to a surplus of $2 billion, compared with a surplus of $4.2 billion in 2003. He also predicted that the current account surplus will narrow to $4.5 billion to $6.0 billion from $8 billion last year.  \par \par \uc2 But Pridiyathorn was concerned about the delay in foreign direct investment, or FDI, inflows.  \par \par \uc2 Violence in southern Thailand since the first quarter of 2004, as well as competition from China and Vietnam, have delayed FDI inflows to possibly next year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said.  \par \par \uc2 "But it's not worrisome as long as we have a current account surplus and high reserves. If we run into a (current account) deficit, and our reserves fall, there will be a great need to have FDI," Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 Ctrl Bk Says Bird Flu Won't Hammer Economy  \par \par \uc2 A new outbreak of avian influenza in Thailand's central provinces shouldn't have any significant impact on the economy because exports of chicken products account for only 1% of the country's total exports, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said.  \par \par \uc2 "We already put the impact of bird flu in our economic model. It will shave no more than half a percentage point off our economic growth this year," Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 Most major poultry buyers abroad still ban the import of raw poultry meat from Thailand, although the import of cooked products is allowed.  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn also said he doesn't expect the reemergence of bird flu to have any significant negative effect on domestic consumption.  \par \par \uc2 Thailand Wednesday confirmed fresh outbreaks of the disease in the central provinces of Ayudhya and Prathum Thani.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bangkok Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266 0744; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ryan Woo [ 08-07-04 1021GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040708e078000gl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
