\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Firmer on stocks, capped by mixed data.  \b0\par\par\uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2004\par 06:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, June 8 (Reuters) - Asian regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strengthened on Tuesday helped by gains in equity markets and\par as oil prices stayed off last week's highs.\par     However, analysts said mixed economic data from across the\par region would likely keep investors from buying too\par aggressively.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        was the lead performer,\par gaining by about a percent to hit a one-week high of 9,265 to\par the dollar.\par     Dealers in Singapore said the rise of the rupiah was partly\par due to higher reserve requirements, funds banks have to\par maintain with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which were announced last week.\par Higher reserves mean banks would have less rupiah to buy\par dollars.\par     The U.S. dollar's recent retreat from highs against the\par euro  and Japanese yen        also supported regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The South Korean won            rose to its highest since\par April 28, before giving up part of those gains on suspected\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar          hit a one-week high. The\par Singapore dollar , Thai baht  and Philippine peso\par   posted modest gains.\par     Thio Chin Lo, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at BNP Paribas in Singapore\par said oil prices still had the potential to remain volatile\par given the risk of terror attacks in the Middle East.\par     "Hence, even though stock markets have started the week on\par a bullish note and oil prices have eased from peaks, the\par uncertain geopolitical landscape continues to leave investors\par in a cautious mood," she said.\par     MIXED DATA\par     Analysts said mixed economic performance, as shown by\par recent data releases, across the region also meant investors\par might avoid taking aggressive directional bets in the\par regionals.\par     Data on Monday showed Taiwan's exports in May had jumped to\par a record $15.71 billion, marking a surprising 39.5 percent\par increase over a year earlier.\par     Taiwan's consumer price index, however, declined by a\par seasonally adjusted 0.33 percent in May from April due to lower\par food prices.\par     Data from South Korea showed output from the retail sector\par shrank in the year through April, reflecting weak consumer\par spending.\par     James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase, said\par the won still had room to head as high as 1,152 to the dollar\par in the near-term.\par  \par     But he added dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities had\par restricted the won's rise.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's soft gross domestic product growth data,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par released on Monday, also came as a surprise. GDP grew 0.8\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in the first quarter, the slowest in the past 10\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarters.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Michael Spencer, chief economist at Deutsche Bank in Hong\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Kong, said in a client note that growth momentum had weakened\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par due to a sharp decline in exports and weak private consumption.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wong Chee Seng, an economist at Singapore's DBS Bank, said\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thai growth was hurt by a contraction of the agriculture\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sector.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Even though agriculture sector accounts for less than 11\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent of total GDP, its repercussion on the economy should\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not be underestimated, as around 43 percent of employment is\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par generated by this sector," he said.\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.61         110.10       +0.45\par  Sing dlr        1.7040         1.7059       +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr      33.477         33.487       +0.03\par  Korean won     1157.00        1159.10       +0.18\par  Baht             40.55          40.55       +0.00\par  Peso             55.78          55.81       +0.04\par  Rupiah         9295.00        9335.00       +0.43\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.61         107.31       -2.10\par  Sing dlr        1.7040         1.6978       -0.36\par  Taiwan dlr      33.477         33.978       +1.50\par  Korean won     1157.00        1192.00       +3.03\par  Baht             40.55          39.59       -2.38\par  Peso             55.78          55.49       -0.52\par  Rupiah         9295.00        8410.00       -9.52.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040608e068000bw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
