\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Thai  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  satisfied with baht.   \b0\par\par\uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2004\par 05:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Jan 15 (Reuters) - The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the rise of the baht has been effective and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at a satisfactory level, Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 "Our \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the other day has been effective and it is now satisfactory. We are more happy with the level of the baht today than the other day," Pridiyathorn told reporters, referring to the baht's brief sharp advance on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra told reporters on Tuesday he believed the baht still did not reflect Thailand's bullish economic fundamentals despite its recent rise against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Thaksin's remarks pushed the baht up to around 38.83 per dollar, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreated sharply later on Tuesday to 38.92 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said the baht was too strong.   \par \par \uc2 The baht traded at around 39.00 per dollar at 0445 GMT on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 "The remarks should effectively put a cap to any further upside retracement on dollar/baht which this morning hit 39.04 on an overall firmer dollar," said Singapore-based research house MMS International.   \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn said he expected Thai economic growth to accelerate in 2004 from 6.3 percent growth projected by analysts for 2003.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue its accommodative monetary policy in maintaining low Thai interest rates, he said.   \par \par \uc2 Economist Thanomsri Fongarun-rung at Phatra Securities said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to assure people it would continue the growth-oriented policies which have helped the economy expand rapidly.   \par \par \uc2 "It is telling people that this year is a better year and you don't need to worry about the business outlook. Interest rates will stay supportive of growth," she said.   \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn said Thailand would post another current account surplus this year. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in October it expected a 2003 current account surplus of $7-8 billion.   \par \par \uc2 Merrill Lynch estimates Thai housing demand will rise between 20 and 30 percent this year and that average capacity utilisation at most major industrial plants has risen to 85-90 percent from 65 percent two years ago.   \par \par \uc2 To avoid a repeat of a housing bubble seen during the run-up to the 1997/98 Asian economic crisis, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has imposed measures to curb excessive supply in the property sector, Thanomsri said.   \par \par \uc2 "It will keep speculation on property shares down because people will know that the Bank of Thailand is on the case," she said. (Reporting by Kitiphong Thaichareon and Trisanat Kongkhunthian, additional reporting by Chawadee Nualkhair).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040115e01f0016c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
