\par\par \b \uc2 Asian stumble would hit global debt market - banker.   \b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2003\par 05:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Nov 10 (Reuters) - The global debt market faces potentially severe disruption if Asian economies falter, forcing central banks to withdraw substantial investments in U.S. Treasuries, a senior Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Tasna Rajatabhothi, an assistant governor at the Bank of Thailand (BOT), told reporters the concern was discussed at a bi-monthly meeting of senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials hosted by the Bank for International Settlements (BIS).   \par \par \uc2 Most of a combined $1.8 trillion of foreign reserves at Asian central banks has been invested in U.S. Treasuries.   \par \par \uc2 "Should Asian economies falter in the future, it could affect every country, including the United States," Tasna said. "This is a concern voiced by some officials."   \par \par \uc2 The BOT official said recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by some Asian countries, including China and \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , were another issue discussed at the meeting.   \par \par \uc2 Tasna said Chinese officials repeated Beijing's policy on the yuan, which has become a political issue in the United States, but gave no further details.   \par \par \uc2 She said Thai officials briefed the meeting on recent BOT measures to curb foreign speculation on the bullish baht, which has appreciated about eight percent against the dollar so far this year.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has limited the amounts of baht non-residents can keep in Thai banks in its bid to discourage them from betting on a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  whose strength has been supported by the country's booming economy.   \par \par \uc2 The BOT has instructed Thai banks to report daily the baht accounts kept by foreigners who are not allowed to keep more than 300 million baht without other underlying business.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031110dzba000b8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
