\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Baht  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  could hurt economy-Thai PM.  \b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2003\par 10:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Oct 10 (Reuters) - Official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the appreciation of the Thai baht could hurt the economy, Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that goes against market forces could put the economy at risk," he told reporters after exporters called on the government to halt the rise of the baht.  \par \par \uc2 The baht has appreciated about 10 percent against the dollar so far this year. Its sharp advance has hurt Thai exporters who asked the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOT) said on Friday it was monitoring increased baht funds parked by non-residents in domestic bank accounts in a bid to restrain foreign speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 BOT deputy governor Thirachai Phuvanatnaranubala told reporters that total outstanding short-term baht funds kept by foreigners in local bank accounts had risen to about 45 billion baht from 10-15 billion baht last month.  \par \par \uc2 Thaksin said his government could not respond to all requests from different economic sectors on the baht issue.  \par \par \uc2 "We are carefully monitoring it and appreciate their problems, but we cannot oblige every request. The Bank of Thailand has the main responsibility while the government occasionally offers its advice," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Thaksin said while the authorities would try to maintain the baht's stability, Thai exporters should try to adjust to its recent fluctuations.  \par \par \uc2 The baht traded at around 39.18/22 at 0842 GMT on Friday, against 39.22 late on Thursday and 43.08 at the end of 2002.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031010dzaa0018r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
