\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -C.banks limit rally, S&P helps.  \b0\par\par\uc2 655 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2003\par 11:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rallied to\par fresh highs on Wednesday buoyed by the U.S. dollar's fall to\par new lows against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but gains were limited on\par suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by central banks.\par     The Japanese yen's        rise through the psychological\par barrier of 110 per dollar, to new three-year highs, had raised\par expectations that central banks in the region might allow some\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthening as well.\par     Dealers suspected central banks bought dollars in South\par Korea and Taiwan. There were also rumours of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bids\par for dollars in Thailand and Singapore.\par     "Most of the actions were sporadic and not very aggressive.\par It suggests they (central banks) are looking to limit the moves\par not reverse the trend," one dealer at a foreign bank in\par Singapore said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The South Korean won            managed to trade near a\par three year high, the Thai baht  hit a new three-year\par high, and the Singapore dollar  reached fresh four-month\par peaks. The Taiwan dollar  also tested levels near a\par one-year high.\par     Standard & Poor's credit rating upgrade for Thailand,\par Indonesia and Malaysia further helped the bullish sentiment.\par For a detailed story\par     "The common theme driving the upgrades is improvements in\par Asian external balance sheets, as persistent trade surpluses\par and rising \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves have reduced the\par vulnerability to financial shocks," said Thio Chin Loo, senior\par analyst at BNP Paribas in Singapore.\par  \par     She said the upgrades would help step up investment flows\par that would keep regional stock markets and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  buoyed.\par     However, she expected central banks to continue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets and limit the rallies.\par     A senior official at South Korea's finance ministry told\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters there had been no change in the government's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign  \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy - a reference to recent dollar-buying  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Korean authorities.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While dealers in Bangkok said rumours of dollar bids from  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 authorities prompted local corporates to cover their short U.S.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar positions, the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it had not  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow the baht's sharp gains.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The strong baht is due to the S&P upgrade. Everything  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 looks good, which we very much welcome. We don't know what we  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 could do," Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia's policy to keep \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weak to help boost exports  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 has come under increasing criticism from the United States and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Europe and the focus has been China's yuan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 virtually pegged at around 8.278 per dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chairman of the U.S. Senate Finance Committee, Charles  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Grassley, on Tuesday sent a letter to the Chinese government,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 threatening action unless the country moves to a flexible  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exchange rate and upholds trade commitments.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan's one-year non-deliverable forward contract  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 retraced some of the recent gains down to around 4,500 points  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to the U.S. dollar. On Tuesday, it had hit record premium above  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5,000 points per U.S. dollar, pricing an appreciation of about  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 six and a half percent.   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0905 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.78       110.47         +0.63\par  Sing dlr      1.7225       1.7236         +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    33.768       33.793         +0.07\par  Korean won   1149.90      1151.10         +0.10\par  Baht           39.29        39.46         +0.43\par  Peso           55.00        55.05         +0.09\par  Rupiah       8365.00      8385.00         +0.24\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.78       118.74         +8.16\par  Sing dlr      1.7224       1.7341         +0.68\par  Taiwan dlr    33.768       34.753         +2.92\par  Korean won   1149.90      1185.80         +3.12\par  Baht           39.29        43.08         +9.65\par  Peso           55.00        53.38         -2.95\par  Rupiah      