\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Ctrl Bk Gov: Strong Baht May Slow Exports Slightly  \b0\par\par\uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2003\par 09:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Wednesday that the baht's recent strength against the dollar was caused by exports outgrowing imports, while debt repayment has slowed due to the sharp decrease in outstanding foreign debt since the 1997 financial crisis.  \par \par \uc2 "The baht may strengthen a little bit further, but wait until imports catch up with exports and the current account balances, then the baht will stabilize," Pridiyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn acknowledged that the strong baht may slow exports "a bit" but said there was "nothing wrong with a strong baht" as long as exports were outpacing imports.  \par \par \uc2 He reiterated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't oppose the market trend and is only trying to limit the day-to-day volatility through recent measures introduced to limit speculative inflows. He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movement in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and hasn't been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  regards the current appreciation of the baht as a natural occurrence of a recovering economy," he told a business luncheon.  \par \par \uc2 However, he warned that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will monitor the ongoing rally in the stock market for any signs of an asset price bubble and will act if necessary.  \par \par \uc2 "So far, we haven't seen any bad signs. If we see, rest assured that we'll take action," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The Stock Exchange of Thailand's main index has risen 63% so far this year, hitting a six-year high recently. Trading volume has also hit record levels in recent weeks, prompting regulatory authorities to warn they would take action against short-term speculators by banning margin lending or net settlement in certain stocks.  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn expressed confidence that there is scope for the economy to improve further on the strong growth so far this year once the global economy improves and private investment kicks in to complement export growth and consumer demand as economic growth drivers.  \par \par \uc2 "The challenge is to translate current growth into a sustainable momentum... and ensure that capacity utilization will increase and private capital investment will gain a strong footing," he said.  \par \par \uc2 He said until this happens, monetary policy will remain accommodative, indicating that the low interest rate environment will be maintained next year.  \par \par \uc2 He noted there were already signs that private investment, which has so far lagged growth in exports and private consumption, has been picking up steam, having risen to 16% of gross domestic product from 11% in 1999.  \par \par \uc2 "Barring any major distractions to the economy from abroad, I expect private investment to come to the limelight soon," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Going forward, Pridiyathorn said he saw three challenges for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : balancing the country's external reliance with domestic strength, ensuring the recovery of commercial bank credit growth and dealing with risks brought about by globalization.  \par \par \uc2 He expressed confidence that the lingering problem of nonperforming loans in the financial system would be tackled following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's proposal to the finance ministry to transfer nonperforming assets that had been used as collateral, from the commercial banks to state-owned asset management agencies and speed up their liquidation. This plan could become effective early next year, if it's approved by the government, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Pridiyathorn said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also monitor an increase in household debt but noted that, at 27% of gross domestic product, it was still low compared with other countries in the region.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jenny Paris, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266 0744; jenny.paris@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Simon Harvey  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031001dza1000ah\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
