\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Ctrl Bk: Baht Up On Dlr Weakness; No  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2003\par 07:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Thursday that the baht's recent strength was mainly due to general dollar weakness, and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 He told reporters that the dollar has weakened around 4% against the yen and the euro since Sept. 19, while the baht has risen only about 1.5% against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The baht is still competitive, moving in line with most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday, the dollar fell to a 38-month low of 39.910 baht as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets put the Group of Seven's weekend endorsement of flexible exchange rates to the test.  \par \par \uc2 At 0550 GMT, the dollar was at THB40.095, marginally up from THB40.075 early Thursday, tracking a mild consolidation in the yen.  \par \par \uc2 "It's clear that there is no speculation in the market now," Prididyathorn said.  \par \par \uc2 The absence of speculation is apparently due to subsiding short-term inflows in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market following a new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rule.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Thailand earlier this month imposed a limit of THB50 million on baht imports by nonresidents for short-term loans to local financial institutions that aren't connected to trade or investment.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Deputy Governor Thirachai Phuvanatnaranubala said Wednesday that liquidity in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that isn't linked to trade or investment has dropped dramatically to $30 million from $200 million last week and around $2.4 billion before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  limit was imposed.  \par \par \uc2 -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; suttinee.yuvejwattana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ryan Woo  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020030925dz9p0006c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
