\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Wary of "lines in the sand".  \b0\par\par\uc2 697 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2003\par 10:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 25 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spent most\par of Thursday in slightly softer ranges, shy of this week's highs\par and watching the Japanese yen ease after threats of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The yen        weakened past 112 per dollar after Japan's\par top financial diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi and others said Japan\par was prepared to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if necessary.\par     Other central banks in the region also seemed uncomfortable\par with the rises in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that have followed the Group\par of Seven's call for more flexible exchange rates on the\par weekend.\par  \par     Asian stock markets were lower, under the influence of the\par decline in the Nikkei average .\par     The Thai baht        stayed around 40.10 per dollar, the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korean won found its gains capped at its three-year high of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1,150 and the Singapore dollar moved in a 1.7330-1.7345  \par \par \uc2 range, having come off Monday's three-month high of 1.7230.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Thursday it had not\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the past 10 days.\par     Other central banks appeared to be following the Thai\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 example of controls on short-term flows, amid signs they had  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 tried to moderate the inflow of foreign capital being raised by  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 domestic institutions without directly buying dollars.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Corporates in Taiwan said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was trying to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ease the upward pressure on the Taiwan dollar by  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 regulating the conversion of overseas bond and share issues.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A source in the South Korean finance ministry said the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 government was in talks with domestic issuers of dollar bonds  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on the need for the issues, as well as the timing and size.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Wednesday, Korean authorities said they might act   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the rising won             which was hurting\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exports, and revealed plans to issue more of the bonds they use  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to sterilise the liquidity generated by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier in the week, an Indian government official said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 petrochemicals maker Reliance Industries Ltd's proposal to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 borrow $500 million overseas would not be approved because the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 government wanted to discourage firms from raising foreign  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 debt.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Asian central banks have put up a robust performance in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the face of dollar weakness/yen strength, and we expect that  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 lines in the sand are being formed more robustly in Asia than  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in Japan," strategists at National Australia Bank said in a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 note.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     They said key levels were 1.7250 for the Singapore dollar,\par 40.00 for the baht, and 1,150 for won.\par     And, with China refusing to bow to demands to make the yuan\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 flexible or let it appreciate, authorities in Japan and in rest  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of Asia will have an excuse to rein in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 they said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Fundamentally, and in line with the policy prescriptions  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of Asian central banks, we believe that there will be very  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 robust support for U.S. dollar/Asian regionals going forward,"  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NAB's report said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the Philippine peso remained near its  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 lows for the week, hitting 55.19 per dollar, with persisting  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 concerns about the overshoot in the fiscal deficit in August.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A poll also showed sliding approval rating and public trust  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo, with support for her  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 slipping to a low of 41 percent.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0805 GMT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     112.14       111.76         -0.34\par  Sing dlr      1.7335       1.7346         +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    33.795       33.760         -0.10\par  Korean won   1151.60      1150.50         -0.10\par  Baht           40.08        40.06         -0.05\par  Peso           55.14        55.12         -0.04\par  Rupiah       8455.00      8435.00         -0.24\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     112.14       118.74         +5.89\par  Sing dlr      1.7335       1.7341         +0.03\par  Taiwan dlr    33.795       34.753 