\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Step back again as rhetoric rises.  \b0\par\par\uc2 704 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2003\par 05:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 25 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  distanced\par themselves further from the week's strong peaks on Thursday as\par the risks of Japanese dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  increased\par along with rising rhetoric from regional central banks.\par     The U.S. dollar was undermined by weak stock markets, yet\par found itself supported against the yen  after Haruhiko\par Kuroda, formerly Japan's top financial diplomat and now a\par special adviser to the prime minister, said Japan was prepared\par to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if necessary.\par     Regional central banks have not been too pleased to see\par their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit multi-month and multi-year peaks in recent\par days, after a Group of Seven weekend meeting called for more\par flexible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regimes.\par     On Wednesday, South Korean authorities said they might act\par against the rising won             which was hurting\par exports, and revealed plans to issue more of the bonds they use\par to sterilise the liquidity generated by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seemed more tolerant of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par gains. Officials said they would not resist baht strength but\par would fight speculation.\par     Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this week to cap the\par Taiwan dollar  at 13-month highs. A newspaper report on\par Thursday stated the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had also refused First\par Financial Holding Co (2892.TW) permission to convert the\par proceeds of a $515 million overseas issue into local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     As the yen eased towards 112 per dollar, the Thai baht\par   was pushed decisively to the weaker side of 40 per\par dollar while the Korean won found gains capped at 1,150.\par  \par     The Singapore dollar        was range-bound after having\par come off a June high of 1.7230 since Monday.\par     "There is going to be continuing pressure from fundamentals\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to appreciate over the next three months,"  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said Ray Farris, markets strategist with Credit Suisse First  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boston.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The main driver though is going to be dollar/yen and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 markets are still undecided about whether it will enter a new  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 range of roughly 110-115 or if it is going to break down to 105  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 or 100."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If dollar/yen breaks down further, then there will be  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 irresistible pressure on dollar/Asia to break lower and it  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 seems unlikely Asian central banks will be able to fully resist  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that pressure," Farris said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KOREA VOLATILITY FALLS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Strategists at JP Morgan said the realised volatility on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the won had fallen to its lowest in a year, despite the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 volatility generated by the G7 meeting.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Taken together, this signals the Bank of Korea's intent to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 smooth the dollar/won downtrend, rather than to reverse it,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 though we believe that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be unable to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 resist the broader regional move and the dollar/won will lag  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rather than buck the trend," the report said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Meanwhile, the popular yen-won cross            was also\par off the week's peak of 10.45, easing to around 10.28.\par     Elsewhere, the Philippine peso        remained near its\par lows for the week, hitting 55.19 per dollar, with persisting\par concerns over the overshoot in the fiscal deficit in August.\par     A poll also showed sliding approval rating and public trust\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo, with support for her  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 slipping to a low of 41 percent.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0310 GMT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     111.84       111.76         -0.07\par  Sing dlr      1.7340       1.7346         +0.03\par  Taiwan dlr    33.764       33.760         -0.01\par  Korean won   1151.10      1150.50         -0.05\par  Baht           40.07        40.06         -0.02\par  Peso           55.06        55.12         +0.11\par  Rupiah       8454.00      8435.00         -0.22\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     111.84       118.74         +6.17\par  Sing dlr      1.7340       1.7341         +0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    33.764       34.753         +2.93\par  Korean won   1151.10      1185.80         +3.01\par  Baht           40.07        43.08         +7.51\par  Peso           55.06        53.38         -3.05\par  Rupiah       8454.00      8940.00         +5.75 ((Editing by\par John Mair; vidya.ranganathan@reuters.com; Reuters Messaging:\par vidya.ranganathan.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870 3090)).\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030925dz9p000ej\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
