\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Thai  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  curb seen delaying baht rally.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Vithoon Amorn  \par \uc2 648 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2003\par 12:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Sept 12 (Reuters) - Efforts by Thailand to curb inflows of hot foreign money to speculate on the baht have sent Asia's most bullish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into retreat, but the impact may be short-lived, analysts said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Thailand (BOT) told domestic banks on Thursday to stop accepting short-term offshore baht from non-residents anticipating further gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 That triggered a baht sell-off early on Friday to a low of around 41.04 per U.S. dollar from 40.44 late on Thursday. The baht later recovered to 40.75 by 1020 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 Deputy BOT governor Thirachai Phuvanatnaranubala said the weaker baht on Friday reflected economic fundamentals and he was happy with its orderly retreat after the bank's move.  \par \par \uc2 "The baht has weakened slightly," he told reporters. "Its orderly adjustment is not necessarily a problem."  \par \par \uc2 "The baht, at this level, largely reflects Thai fundamentals. Our management of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have any specific target for it."  \par \par \uc2 The baht has gained around 5.3 percent versus the U.S. dollar so far in 2003, driven by strong economic growth seen at around six percent this year and a high current account surplus.  \par \par \uc2 HOT STOCKS  \par \par \uc2 The gain has attracted foreign investors, who have also targeted a booming Thai share market up 59 percent this year.  \par \par \uc2 The new restriction means non-residents would not be permitted to keep more than 50 million offshore baht in Thailand for periods of less than three months without normal underlying business.  \par \par \uc2 Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  prohibited domestic banks from lending securities to offshore players in what it said was a precautionary move to limit future short selling of the baht.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently in recent months to slow the baht's rise but \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to breach the key psychological level of 40 baht per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 With Thailand running a current account surplus of around six percent of GDP, UBS \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Bhanu Baweja said he saw the baht at 40.50 over three months and at 39 baht in 12 months.  \par \par \uc2 "We believe the measure will change nothing in the trend of the THB/USD, and consider any weakness in the THB as temporary," he said in a commentary on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at the Bank of Ayudhya said he also saw no lasting impact from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions.  \par \par \uc2 "It should have some short-term weakening effect, but with a heavy flow of funds into the Thai stock market, we will probably see it back to around 40.25 a month from now," he said.  \par \par \uc2 SPECULATION THE TARGET  \par \par \uc2 Thirachai said the average daily amount of offshore baht on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, mostly hot money betting on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rising, surged to around $2.1 billion this month from an average $1.5 billion during May-August and $900 million early this year.  \par \par \uc2 He said the BOT was not trying to stop a baht appreciation driven by strong domestic growth, just speculation.  \par \par \uc2 "We control only short-term imports of offshore baht without underlying business, but do not restrict imports of dollars and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  irrespective of how short their maturity," Thirachai said on radio.  \par \par \uc2 "In managing our exchange rate, we will not try to move a big trunk with a small stick," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund urged Asian countries on Thursday to adopt more flexible exchange rates. The fund said it would be helpful for countries with managed-float \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , like \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  less in the market.  \par \par \uc2 Since July, the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has relaxed exchange controls to allow domestic institutions to invest up to $2.4 billion in foreign debt instruments, a move aimed at helping absorb a huge surplus of funds.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030912dz9c003gq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
