\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Baht drops on new cenbank rules.  \b0\par\par\uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2003\par 05:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganthan\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 12 (Reuters) - The Thai baht fell sharply\par on Friday morning after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sought to limit\par speculative investors chasing it higher by capping the amount\par of short-term funds non-residents could park in the country.\par     That, and anxiety over dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japan,\par put a floor under the U.S. dollar in Asia, as it also recovered\par against the euro after the second anniversary of the September\par 11 attacks passed uneventfully.\par     "Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remain bid. But central banks either\par through direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or through regulation, as in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , are going to seek to have their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par competitively realigned," said Michael Jansen, markets\par strategist with National Australia Bank, Sydney.\par     The baht        dropped over one percent from Thursday's\par levels to the weaker side of 41 per dollar in morning deals.\par The baht had been testing 14-month highs of 40.20, a break of\par which would have taken it to three-year highs.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Late on Thursday, the Bank of Thailand said banks could not\par accept more than 50 million baht from non-residents seeking to\par park funds in the country for less than three months. It said\par it wanted to curtail speculative inflows betting on baht\par strength.\par     "The new restriction reflects more on ongoing BOT efforts\par to manage short-term capital flows to curb \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility\par than on conscious efforts to manage baht strength," James\par Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan, said in a note.\par     Last week, the Bank of Thailand banned local banks from\par lending securities to offshore players, describing the measure\par as a defence against speculative attacks on the baht in the\par future.\par     YEN INFLUENCE\par     The Singapore dollar        fell early, along with the\par baht, to the weaker side of 1.75 but later pared some of that\par loss.\par     The steady yen        was the main influence for the rest\par of Asia, keeping the Taiwan dollar from firming despite the\par recovery in stock markets, which attracts foreign investment.\par Markets in Korea were closed for holidays. They reopen on\par Monday.\par    Jansen said the Bank of Japan might succeed in pushing the\par yen down to 118 or even 119 per dollar over the next couple of\par weeks.\par     "That will weaken Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , because obviously if\par the yen is weakening there will be a form of competitive\par revaluation in the region, particularly in Korea and maybe in\par Singapore and Thailand," he said.\par     The Philippine peso        was volatile, dropping as low as\par 55.15 in early deals and then climbing back above 55 per\par dollar.\par     Despite a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  measure this week that barred\par residents from buying dollars to invest in dollar-denominated\par bonds, traders said there was heavy interest to buy dollars\par below the pivotal 55 per dollar level. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.\par DOLLAR AT 0245 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.05       117.08         +0.03\par  Sing dlr      1.7487       1.7476         -0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    34.093       34.090         -0.01\par  Korean won   1170.00      1170.00          0.00\par  Baht           40.88        40.44         -1.06\par  Peso           54.97        55.03         +0.11\par  Rupiah       8470.00      8455.00         -0.18\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.05       118.74         +1.44\par  Sing dlr      1.7487       1.7341         -0.83\par  Taiwan dlr    34.093       34.753         +1.94\par  Korean won   1170.00      1185.80         +1.35\par  Baht           40.88        43.08         +5.39\par  Peso           54.97        53.38         -2.89\par  Rupiah       8470.00      8940.00         +5.55 ((Editing by\par John Mair; vidya.ranganathan@reuters.com; Reuters Messaging:\par vidya.ranganathan.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870 3090)).\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030912dz9c000jq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
