\par\par \b \uc2  APEC Supports Bond Mkt Cooperation Despite  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Divisions \b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2003\par 14:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  PHUKET, Thailand -(Dow Jones)- Asia Pacific finance ministers Friday agreed to promote a more integrated regional bond market that will eventually lead to cross-border issues, even as they rebuffed calls to remove protective mechanisms in their exchange rate regimes. \par \par \uc2  In a joint statement issued at the end of a two-day meeting of the Asia Pacific Economic Cooperation forum, finance ministers said they will work together to achieve well-developed bond markets. \par \par \uc2  "We acknowledged that further cooperation is necessary to attain domestic and regional conditions which are essential to facilitate cross-border bond market activities," the ministers said in the statement. \par \par \uc2  They also expressed support for an initiative by Thailand, Japan and South Korea to issue new products - such as long-term, local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  denominated debt instruments, derivatives and asset-backed securities - to be traded within the region. \par \par \uc2  Integration of the regional bond market was highlighted as a key part of the APEC talks agenda by the Thai hosts, but was overshadowed by a lengthy debate over appropriate exchange rate policies. \par \par \uc2  The 21 APEC ministers ended their meeting accepting a U.S.-inspired call for gradual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -policy reform but offered no specifics on how they might pick up the pace. \par \par \uc2  But without a clear commitment toward \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility, it's uncertain how an integrated regional bond market could take off. \par \par \uc2  Thailand itself said it's dropped plans to issue baht-denominated bonds offshore and will only offer carefully regulated onshore bonds to nonresident investors to avoid arming potential \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators with baht assets. \par \par \uc2  Like other central banks in the region, Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem exchange rate volatility, effectively slowing the pace of the baht's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have boosted regional \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which at more than $1 trillion equal almost half of the world's total. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow, who campaigned to get APEC members to commit to a process of greater exchange rate flexibility during the two days, said market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be kept to a minimum. \par \par \uc2  "The management of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at unnatural rates distorts markets, tending toward beggar-thy-neighbor policies, and encourages protectionism," Snow said. \par \par \uc2  In June, 11 central banks from the Asia Pacific region agreed to pool a small portion of their reserves to set up an Asian Bond Fund that will invest in regional bonds, in a bid to maintain Asian savings within the region. \par \par \uc2  The $1-billion fund will initially invest in dollar-denominated sovereign and quasi-sovereign bonds, and possibly in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds at a later stage. \par \par \uc2  Market participants believe the issuance of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds for cross-border trading in the region is still a long way off as several technical hurdles must be overcome, such as tax and settlement barriers. \par \par \uc2  APEC ministers said they will promote the development of securitization and credit guarantee markets that will enhance the efficiency of regional bond markets, but fell short of outlining specific steps to facilitate cross-border trading. \par \par \uc2  -By Jenny Paris, Dow Jones Newswires; 661-929 4817; jenny.paris@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030905dz95000v0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
