\par\par \b \uc2 Thailand's turn to lead Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  again?  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Vidya Ranganathan  \par \uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2003\par 06:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Sept 3 (Reuters) - The Thai baht has come full circle.  \par \par \uc2 Six years after a de facto devaluation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sparked the Asian financial crisis, Thailand appears to be front-running a campaign to ease capital controls in Asia and tolerate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains.  \par \par \uc2 At a 13-month high of 40.83 against the dollar on Wednesday, the baht replaced the Indonesian rupiah as Asia's best performing tradeable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.  \par \par \uc2 It has risen 5.5 percent nominally this year and more than 4 percent in trade-weighted terms since July.  \par \par \uc2 An upgrade of Thailand's ratings by Fitch vindicated the rally, which has been backed by the country's improving domestic and external growth.  \par \par \uc2 Within the country, Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra seemed to be winning the familiar war of words between the government, which forecasts the baht in a range of 39 to 40 by the end of the year, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which wants slower moves.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand Deputy Governor Thirachai Phuvanatnaranubala on Wednesday urged the countries of the Asia-Pacific region to follow the Thai example and ease capital controls.  \par \par \uc2 "Maybe the first crack in the dam of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength is being seen in \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said David Simmonds, markets strategist with the Royal Bank of Scotland.  \par \par \uc2 Seen in the context of Thaksin's role in piloting the Asian regional bond fund, which was launched in June, it all fits into place, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 "Thailand is pushing its political agenda in terms of leading Asia through the Asian bond fund," said James Malcolm, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with JP Morgan.  \par \par \uc2 "They need to be seen as moving ahead of other people on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because it is so undervalued and its fair value is probably near 37-38."  \par \par \uc2 MYSTIFYING MOVE  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the government forecasts for the baht to rise to 39 per dollar will be right, even if that does not happen as soon as the end of the year.  \par \par \uc2 Thailand recently exited an IMF loan programme, after repaying the debt two years in advance, and the baht's rise has not been disrupted by rate cuts in June and by a move to allow domestic institutions to invest heavily overseas.  \par \par \uc2 The attractiveness of the stock market , which has been drawing a torrent of foreign investment, the rising exports to China and the rebound in tourism after the outbreak of Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome (SARS) all bode well for the baht, analysts at Standard Chartered Bank said in a note.  \par \par \uc2 Implied volatility on baht options has been rising along with rumours that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively and seeking ways to rein in the appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 Markets were confused on Tuesday by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement that it had banned local banks from lending securities to offshore players.  \par \par \uc2 The baht retreated, in a knee-jerk reaction, before markets realised such a ban is traditionally a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  defence mechanism aimed at preventing foreigners from short-selling securities to bet on a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falling.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said markets were misreading the measure, which probably was aimed at developing Thailand's repo segment.  \par \par \uc2 "This means the offshore markets cannot have access to the Thai repo market and cannot park their money onshore through repos," said Sameer Goel, markets strategist at Bank of America.  \par \par \uc2 "It is irrelevant to the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and it does not make that much of a difference because one can still go short dollar/baht and lend the baht onshore via the swap market."   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030903dz93000y5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
