\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk: Doesn't Need To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2003\par 09:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula reiterated Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently to curb the baht's strength against the dollar because there's no immediate need to do so. \par \par \uc2  "Why would we have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?" Pridiyathorn asked reporters rhetorically. He said he hadn't consulted with the department responsible for financial market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet Tuesday, however. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and government officials have said repeatedly in recent days that investment inflows were attracted naturally to a growing economy, which is why the baht has been strengthening. \par \par \uc2  But while government officials have advertised the baht's uptrend as confirmation of confidence in the economy and their policies, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stressed that it is monitoring speculative flows and is prepared to act if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have said suspected agents of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been supporting the dollar at low points in recent days but not chasing it higher. Pridiyathorn sometimes says that buying dollars for reserves or to stem excessive volatility driven by speculation doesn't constitute \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0258 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 41.025 baht, down from a late morning high of THB41.050, but remaining in an expected range of THB40.900, a 13-month low, to THB41.100. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar ran up from around the low in early trade when heavy importer buying of euros triggered dollar short-covering. Baht holders still buy dollars first before snapping up euros. \par \par \uc2  The afternoon easing in the dollar wasn't a result of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments, a dealer at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  "Once the short-dollar positions were covered, and investors saw the dollar fail to move higher, they begin to sell again," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to move gradually lower amid broad dollar weakness and strong Thai economic data. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand is expected to continue to buy dollars on weakness and to closely monitor speculative activity, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  lightly at key dollar support points whenever the baht appreciates more quickly than other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Atchana Waiquamdee, senior director of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's domestic economic policy department, told a Cabinet meeting Tuesday not to worry about the baht's movements, because the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength reflected economic conditions and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was monitoring markets closely. \par \par \uc2  Sansanee Nakpong, deputy government spokeswoman, told reporters after the Cabinet meeting that Atchana said core inflation - which excludes volatile food and energy prices - was at zero in August compared with last year, but this was due to excessive supply, not weak demand. \par \par \uc2  The current situation doesn't constitute deflation, Atchana said, which is characterized by a long period of falling consumer prices caused by weak demand. \par \par \uc2  In theory, if prices continued to fall, the 14-day repurchase market target rate could fall again from the current level of 1.25%, but it shouldn't have any impact on the general economic situation, Atchana said. \par \par \uc2  She noted that deflation is usually defined as extended subzero inflation as measured by the consumer price index, and the headline CPI was up 2.2% on year in August due to higher oil and fruit and vegetable prices. \par \par \uc2  The commerce ministry said Monday that core inflation was held down by falling rents as low interest rates spurred home buying. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Ryan Woo \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030902dz92000ee\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
