\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Focus on Snow visit, baht rises.  \b0\par\par\uc2 784 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 2003\par 10:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 1 (Reuters) - The Thai baht        eclipsed\par its regional counterparts with a rise to 13-month highs on\par Monday afternoon, as most traders focused on U.S. Secretary\par John Snow's visit to Asia and likely discussions on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par policy.\par     The baht rose past 41 per dollar even as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par tried to limit its gains after a bullish government forecast\par for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The baht extended a three-week long sharp rally to 40.95, a\par July 2002 high, after Finance Minister Suchart Jaovisidha said\par on Friday he expected it to rise to 39-40 per dollar by the end\par of 2003. It was quoted at around 41.20 in late Asian trade on\par Friday and has risen nearly three percent in three weeks.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which last week admitted it had been\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and said it would curb speculative flows,\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  verbally again on Monday.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor\par Pridiyathorn Devakula said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market should heed only\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy on the baht.\par     In a note to clients, UBS said the yen, baht and Korean won\par have appreciated by 4.9 percent, 2.5 percent and 1.8 percent\par respectively in trade-weighted terms so far in this quarter.\par  \par     It added that there were near-term risks for a fall in some\par of the regionals.\par     "Given the weak state of their domestic economies, less\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 valid for Thailand, and the one sided nature of market  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 positioning, the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  becomes very real for  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the short term," UBS said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets were underpricing the risk from North Korea's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 nuclear plans and the rise in valuations during the recent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 equity rallies, the note said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SNOW VISITS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose modestly but underperformed the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 yen as traders awaited word from Snow, who was in Tokyo on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen was off Friday's three-month high of 116.15,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 but stayed on the higher side of 117, finding support after  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese authorities revealed they had not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets believe Snow is likely to call upon Asian  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 countries, particularly China, to absorb some of the U.S.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar's weakness and be more flexible about letting their  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciate.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     U.S. Treasury officials said Snow had not discussed the\par revaluation of any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at a breakfast meeting in Tokyo.\par     Still, the Singapore dollar        was range-bound after\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 failing to get past 1.75 in offshore weekend deals, but the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan dollar rose to a year high as the Taiwan stock  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 market hit 15-month peaks.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won             was slightly higher, the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine peso struggled around the key 55 level, torn  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 between persisting political worries and the government's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 warnings against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  speculation.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Month-end pressure from commercial dollar demand on the\par rupiah eased, allowing it to rise past 8,500, to an 8,460 high.\par     Cliff Tan, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and interest rates strategist at\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Citigroup, said that as markets grew confident about the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 comfort of Japanese authorities with the yen's rally, Asian  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would follow it higher.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think some of the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have a bit to catch  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 up with the yen, so this underperformance may not last for the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 week," Tan said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lehman Brothers said the Snow visit was unlikely to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dramatically alter the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  habits of Asian  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 policymakers.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "But, with the backdrop for Asian capital markets  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 significantly improved, Asian policymakers should be  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 increasingly more sympathetic if Treasury Secretary Snow  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expressed a preference for less \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies," it  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said in a note sent on Monday and written last week.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We don't expect huge revelations in next week's round of  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy sound bytes but we'd view the Asia visit as a modest  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 upside risk to our long-standing bullish Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  view."  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0835 GMT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.64       117.06         +0.36\par  Sing dlr      1.7545       1.7565         +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr    34.112       34.170         +0.17\par  Korean won   1175.30      1178.20         +0.25\par  Baht           40.94        41.19         +0.61\par  Peso           54.96        55.02         +0.11\par  Rupiah       8460.00      8515.00         +0.65\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.64       118.74         +1.80\par  Sing dlr      1.7545       1.7341         -1.16\par  Taiwan dlr    34.112       34.753         +1.88\par  Korean won   1175.30      1185.80         +0.89\par  Baht           40.94        43.08         +5.23\par  Peso           54.96        53.38         -2.87\par  Rupiah       8460.00      8940.00         +5.67.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030901dz910021b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
