\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Thai c.bank monitors baht, seeks to slow rallies. \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 2003\par 09:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Aug 28 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOT) hinted on Thursday it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the baht's sharp gains against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  A bank director said the BOT was monitoring the sharp rise of the baht closely in a bid to try to keep it from getting too strong against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now closely monitoring the baht," Chakramon Phasukvanich told reporters. The baht "has been appreciating, but it has not gained to the extent that it could have," he said without elaboration. \par \par \uc2  The baht rose 0.33 percent against the dollar overnight and has risen about 4.65 percent against the greenback so far this year. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra conceded on Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could probably do little to stem the baht's hefty gains in the past week, saying he believed its rallies reflected the quickly growing domestic economy. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Thailand's current manage-float policy is designed for keeping the baht stable," Thaksin told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "But it is clear that our economy is very strong which convinces people that the baht will remain strong, a fact that is hard to resist." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Thaksin's comments did not help \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to slow baht's rise, which could hurt Thai exports. \par \par \uc2  "BOT is said to have come in via direct onshore to control damage from PM Thaksin's comments: the pair recovers from 41.09 low to 41.14," MMS International in Singapore said in a research note. \par \par \uc2  "The BOT is now letting the market know it shouldn't get too ahead of itself." \par \par \uc2  The baht traded at around 41.17 per dollar at 0719 GMT on Thursday after firming to around 41.09 shortly after Thaksin's comments. \par \par \uc2  Another senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Thursday the baht was still competitive with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite its recent hefty rise against the dollar. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030828dz8s00eo5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
