\par\par \b \uc2  Markets uneasy as Thai baht hits 13-month high. \b0\par\par\uc2 192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 2003\par 03:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     0100 GMT -- Thai baht        extends gains to a 13-month\par high and the Singapore dollar pares some of the previous day's\par losses, raising market caginess about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \par  - Foreign investment inflows into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remain strong\par and the authorities have said they do not mind the gains.\par Simultaneously, they have eased rules on capital outflows.\par  \par  - Market choosing to test higher baht levels in offshore\par deals, post-Asian trading, indicates nervousness, traders said.\par  \par  - Baht quoted at 41.14/17, having risen from near 41.30\par late on Wednesday.\par  \par  - Japan's unease with the rising yen  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a risk to bullish baht positions,\par traders say, since a big yen move can drag Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par along.\par  \par  - The Singapore dollar  is off Wednesday's two-week\par lows but stays on the weaker side of 1.75.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Markets await a Singaporean parliament debate on proposed\par cuts to employer contributions to the city-state's pension\par scheme, and measures to cushion the impact on consumers.\par  \par  - Cuts reinforce market opinion that as the government\par fights to revive the economy it will not tolerate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strength.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030828dz8s002mn\par }\page {\p