\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Up; Off High As Importers,Oil Cos Buy Dlrs \b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2003\par 13:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht ended slightly higher against the dollar Tuesday on optimism the buoyant local economy would continue to strengthen, but dollar buying by oil companies and importers capped its gains. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 41.37 baht at the end of the Asian session, down from THB41.40 at the Asian close Monday - but off an overnight low of THB41.29. \par \par \uc2  The baht surged to a one-year high of THB41.34 against the dollar Monday, boosted by Friday's rating upgrades of top Thai banks by Moody's Investors Service, as well as a stronger yen. \par \par \uc2  Analysts believe rating agencies are poised to upgrade Thailand's credit ranking, which would further drive gains for the baht. Some forecast a 6% rise by year-end to THB39 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  They say Thailand is well-positioned to benefit from an expected recovery in the U.S. economy and - to some extent - Japanese consumption, which would continue to lure big foreign investors to the Southeast Asian nation. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened around THB41.30-THB41.35. Demand from importers and oil companies pushed it to an intraday high of THB41.42 around midday. The weaker yen also helped support the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  But Japanese unit recovered its footing subsequently - lifting the baht to a firmer close. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but is monitoring the movements closely. \par \par \uc2  "The baht is quite stable moving in a range of THB41.38 baht to THB41.41 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but we're keeping an eye on movements," Tasna Rajatabhothi, assistant governor for financial market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the dollar open between THB41.20 and THB41.50 Wednesday, subject to the movements of the yen, a regional trendsetter. \par \par \uc2  Thai government bonds ended slightly lower Tuesday, tracking overnight weakness in U.S. Treasurys, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Some mutual funds also reduced their holdings of government bonds because of market volatility to park their money in higher-yielding assets such as corporate bonds, they added. \par \par \uc2  After rallying in the first half of the year on strong liquidity in the financial system, Thai bonds have languished since August. \par \par \uc2  Market players are worried that demand for Thai debt will fall after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday said it approved $2.45 billion of investment in overseas securities by local big investors such as life insurance firms, mutual funds and provident funds. \par \par \uc2  Concerns over a higher supply of state enterprise bonds next month also hurt sentiment. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the government bond due December 2008 finished up a tad at 2.02%, compared with 2.00% at the last close, according to the Thai Bond Dealing Center. \par \par \uc2  The issue due November 2011 ended at 2.75%, compared with Monday's close of 2.70%. \par \par \uc2  Money market interest rates ended little changed, as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support in the repurchase market helped limit the weight of excess financial system liquidity partially stemming from the baht's strength. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market     Term            Tuesday           Monday\par Interbank  Overnight/Late  1.10000%          1.10000%\par Repurchase Overnight/Close 1.09375%          1.12500%\par            14-Day          1.25000%          1.25000%\par            1-Month         1.25000%          1.25000%\par            3-Month         no activity       no activity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Supunnabul Suwannakij and Suttinee Yuvejwattana, Dow Jones\par Newswires; 662 266 0744; supunnabul.suwannakij@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Edited by Bernice Tang\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030826dz8q000r5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
