\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mostly strong, Singapore dlr down. \b0\par\par\uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2003\par 11:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 22 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar recoiled\par from a two-month high on Friday on fears the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par set to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but the South Korean won and the Taiwan\par dollar were pulled higher by the strength of the yen against\par the dollar.\par     The won                   ended local trade at its\par strongest in 13 months. Players ignored data showing the\par economy was in recession in the first half and focused instead\par on an expected second-half rebound.\par     That optimism prompted buying in the local stock market\par   where foreign investors bought a net $289 million worth\par of shares on Friday.\par     In Taiwan, another economy which has reported negative\par second-quarter GDP growth, the local dollar  rose to\par 11-month highs, despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as\par exporters sold the U.S. dollar.\par     Financial markets in the Philippines, where the peso\par has been falling towards record lows, were closed for a local\par holiday. Trade would resume on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The peso ended\par Thursday's local session at 55.265 per dollar, a record closing\par low.\par     C.BANK CHECKS\par     The Singapore dollar rose to a high of 1.7330 per U.S.\par dollar in offshore trade, its highest since June 20, but pulled\par back this morning after dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par Singapore called up some banks to check rates.\par     That also made players in other Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par wary of the risk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities wanting to\par protect export competitiveness.\par     Bhanu Baweja said Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were gaining because\par they are perceived to have a high correlation to global growth,\par but central banks in the region were still not confident over\par the global outlook.\par     "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is not going to change\par tremendously the direction \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are going, but they are\par not going to get out of the way completely," he said.\par     The Thai baht        held around a one-month high, but\par players were wary of pushing through the 41.45 per dollar level\par because they feared \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The baht stalled twice at the 41.45 level in July and three\par times at an 11-month high of 41.40 in June, largely because of\par suspected Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Indonesian rupiah        came off a one-month high hit\par on Thursday, as some foreign banks booked profits on the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent gains, prompting other players to unwind long\par rupiah positions. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0846 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.83       117.95         +0.10\par  Sing dlr      1.7451       1.7401         -0.29\par  Taiw