\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Mostly stronger, Sing dlr pulls back. \b0\par\par\uc2 719 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2003\par 06:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 22 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar\par retreated from a two-month high early on Friday on fears the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was readying to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but other Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were pulled higher after the yen hit a one-month\par high against the dollar.\par     Data confirming the South Korea economy was in recession in\par the first half of the year was ignored by the won\par  , which was pushed to seven-month highs by foreign\par investors more interested in an expected second half rebound.\par     In Taiwan, another economy which has reported negative\par second quarter GDP growth, the local dollar  rose to\par 11-month highs, despite the efforts of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as\par exporters sold the U.S. dollar.\par     Financial markets in the Philippines, where the peso has\par been slumping towards record lows, were closed for a local\par holiday. Trade would resume on Monday. The peso ended\par Thursday's local session at 55.265 per dollar, a record closing\par low.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     MAS CHECKS\par     The Singapore rose to a high of 1.7329 per U.S. dollar in\par offshore trade, its highest since June 20, but had fallen back\par about one cent by late morning.\par  \par     Dealers said early calls by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par Singapore to check rates with some banks caused the pull back.\par     That also made players in other Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par wary of the risk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities sensitive to\par protecting export competitiveness.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains also counter the easier monetary policy\par stances many central banks have adopted this year.\par     Craig Chan, an analyst at Forecast Ltd, said the Singapore\par dollar has gained on a trade-weighted basis recently, and that\par was why the market believed the risk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was high.\par     "It's a policy that continues to be implemented by all\par central banks in the region," he said.\par     "Any policy tightening through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par particularly of concern here in Singapore, where the government\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has only recently announced some cost cutting measures," he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said, referring to the planned cut in pension contributions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par made by employers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, Chan said central banks across the region might\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par only be able to hold back the gains temporarily, given the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressure from equity-related inflows and a build up of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par structural plays targetting strong growth in Asia amid a global\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BAHT WARY\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  was around a one-month high, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players were wary of pushing through the 41.45 per dollar level\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par because they feared \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  beyond there.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht stalled three times at an 11-month high of 41.40\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in June, largely because of suspected Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BOT Deputy Governor Thirachai Phuvanatnaranubala said on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday the additional easing of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  controls\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this week should reduce the cost of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's efforts\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to slow the baht's gains through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision to let domestic fund\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par managers invest in offshore debt instruments abroad was likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to be followed by other central banks in the region.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the announcement was designed to ease upward\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressure on the baht, which has risen by over four percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the dollar since April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, David Simmonds, strategist at Royal Bank of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Scotland in Singapore, said the impact on the baht would only\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be temporary.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I don't see a constant outflow in debt issues, once the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limits are met that flow will cease," he said. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. DOLLAR AT 0306 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.82       117.95         +0.11\par  Sing dlr      1.7421       1.7401         -0.11\par  Taiwan dlr    34.179       34.238         +0.17\par  Korean won   1170.40      1173.00         +0.22\par  Baht           41.52        41.54         +0.06\par  Peso           55.27        55.27         -0.01\par  Rupiah       8410.00      8375.00         -0.42\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.82       118.74         +0.78\par  Sing dlr      1.7421       1.7341         -0.46\par  Taiwan dlr    34.179       34.753         +1.68\par  Korean won   1170.40      1185.80         +1.32\par  Baht           41.52        43.08         +3.77\par  Peso           55.27        53.38         -3.42\par  Rupiah       8410.00      8940.00         +6.30.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030822dz8m007pz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
