\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED - CORRECTED-Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Peso weakens, rupiah worried. \b0\par\par\uc2 746 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2003\par 11:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In Singapore story "Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -Peso weakens, rupiah worried"\par please read in paragraph 10 ... "Singapore's Straits Times index\par closed down slightly on Friday, ending a run of seven stronger closes."\par ... "Singapore's Straits Times index        made a late recovery to\par post a small gain..." (Corrects market move)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A corrected story follows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  By Vidya Ranganathan \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 15 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso hit a five month low on Friday, one day after a court ordered a year-long suspension of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials including Governor Rafael Buenaventura over the closure of a commercial bank in 2000. \par \par \uc2  Security worries ahead of Indonesia's National Day on Sunday and in the wake of the arrest of Muslim militant leader Hambali kept regional sentiment cautious. \par \par \uc2  The peso  fell as far as 55.10 per dollar, stopping short of a March low of 55.16, with some traders suspecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars at that level. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the breach of the pivotal 55 per dollar level. \par \par \uc2  "The peso is the exception to the strengthening trend in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Thio Chin Loo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with BNP Paribas. \par \par \uc2  "The court ruling is causing some investor confidence erosion. It throws open questions about policy continuity and leadership succession issues and that's negative for the peso." \par \par \uc2  The ruling cannot take effect until all appeals were exhausted, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the officials would remain in their jobs while the legal process played out. \par \par \uc2  Other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied, supported by rising stock markets and some more improvement in economic data in the United States. The dollar steadied in Asian trade after weakening in response to the major power outages in the United States. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar  rose past 1.75 per dollar to its strongest level\par since July 28, while the Thai baht        was boosted when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the baht was not too strong.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht hit a one-month high of 41.58 per dollar. In June and July the\par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent the baht rising beyond 41.40 per\par baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore's Straits Times index  closed down slightly on Friday, ending\par a run of seven stronger closes. On Thursday, the STI hit a 13-month\par high.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korean markets were closed for the Liberation Day holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RUPIAH WARY\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah  was stronger than Thursday, but traders were\par wary of pushing the rupiah higher ahead of National Day celebrations on\par the long holiday weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Security risks were pushed to the fore after the capture in Thailand of\par Hambali, the suspected mastermind of the bomb blasts in Bali last\par October.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The fear of a potential terrorist strike in the upcoming National Day\par celebrations is keeping the rupiah a bit defensive," Thio said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesian President Megawati Sukarnoputri made no reference to Hambali\par in her speech to parliament on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But analysts said his capture would amplify the security concerns in\par the region, which have been rising since a failed mutiny in the\par Philippines at the end of July and last week's bomb blast in a Jakarta\par hotel\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "One can read the Hambali capture in two ways," said James Malcolm,\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with JP Morgan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It is certainly good from the medium to longer term perspective, but\par it gives you ongoing concerns about security issues and terror attacks\par and whether they want to protest this on National Day," he said.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0825 GMT Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen     118.96       119.28         +0.27\par   Sing dlr      1.7482       1.7506         +0.14\par   Taiwan dlr    34.358       34.387         +0.08\par   Korean won   1178.00      1176.50         -0.13\par   Baht           41.63        41.67         +0.11\par   Peso           55.06        54.93         -0.24\par   Rupiah       8532.00      8552.00         +0.23\par   Change on year\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par   Japan yen     118.96       118.74         -0.18\par   Sing dlr      1.7482       1.7341         -0.81\par   Taiwan dlr    34.358       34.753         +1.15\par   Korean won   1178.00      1185.80         +0.66\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Baht 41.63 43.08 +3.50 Peso 55.06 53.38 -3.05 Rupiah 8532.00 8940.00\par +4.78 ((Reporting by Vidya Ranganathan, editing by John Mair;\par 