\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Waiting on Fed, Sing dlr easier. \b0\par\par\uc2 750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2003\par 11:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 11 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar steadied\par after some early falls on Monday following a government\par downgrade of the country's 2003 growth forecast, while the\par Indonesian rupiah extended its recovery after last week's hotel\par bombing.\par     Overall, traders avoided taking aggressive positions in\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy\par meeting on Tuesday and key U.S. data this week.\par     "With (U.S.) summer holidays starting, this is not a week\par to have a strong view, not at least until we hear what the Fed\par has to say," said Philip Wee, strategist at Singapore's DBS\par Bank.\par     Most analysts do not expect any change in U.S. rates this\par week. Wee said the market would like to hear more about\par economic recovery prospects and deflation risks that the Fed\par had been debating since last November.\par     U.S. data this week includes July retail sales on\par Wednesday, and the June trade balance on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Friday is\par busy, with July consumer prices and industrial production\par reports and consumer sentiment figures for August to be\par released.\par     SINGAPORE GROWTH DOWNGRADED\par     The Singapore dollar        eased as far as 1.7584 per U.S.\par dollar in early trade, before recovering to be flat. On Friday,\par it had traded at 1.7525, its highest since late July.\par     Singapore Prime Minister Goh Chok Tong announced the growth\par forecast downgrade to zero to one percent, from 0.5 to 2.5\par percent, on Friday evening.\par     Final second quarter GDP data on Monday showed the economy\par had contracted by an annualised 11.4 percent from the first\par quarter, largely because of the fallout from SARS. The data was\par little changed from preliminary figures released last month.\par     "The full year forecast was a little bit lower than the\par market generally have been expecting," said David Simmonds,\par strategist at Royal Bank of Scotland in Singapore.\par     "That said, I am sure there's a preference on part of the\par authorities here to be a little bit on the side of caution," he\par said, adding the growth estimate could be revised up if\par expectations of a better second half are met.\par     Echoing his views, dealers said some long-term players were\par spotted buying the Singapore dollar on the weaker side of\par 1.7580 per dollar. The yen's rise to three-week highs against\par the U.S. dollar  and euro           also helped.\par     Influenced by the Singapore dollar's early losses, the Thai\par baht  eased a touch to 41.91 per dollar, before bouncing\par back to test 41.80, a level it also tested on Friday. The baht\par spent most of June and July on the stronger side of 41.80 but\par found its gains blocked by Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \par     Baht trade was limited ahead of Tuesday's public holiday,\par dealers said.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        continued to edge higher,\par reclaiming ground lost after last week's bombing of a hotel in\par Jakarta that saw it weaken beyond 8,700 per dollar.\par     The rupiah was around 8,530 per dollar, with mostly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore players spotted covering short rupiah positions they\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were caught holding after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's dollar sales to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par protect the rupiah last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, dealers said there was caution about chasing the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah too high given security and political concerns ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia's national day on Sunday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso  hit 54.89 per dollar, its lowest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in about a week, weighed down by higher corporate demand for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars. Dealers in Manila said a seasonal August/September\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise in imports was expected to keep the peso under pressure.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0815 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.63       118.87         +0.20\par  Sing dlr      1.7550       1.7548         -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    34.384       34.415         +0.09\par  Korean won   1179.10      1181.10         +0.17\par  Baht           41.83        41.88         +0.12\par  Peso           54.84        54.71         -0.24\par  Rupiah       8530.00      8565.00         +0.41\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.63       118.74         +0.09\par  Sing dlr      1.7550       1.7341         -1.19\par  Taiwan dlr    34.384       34.753         +1.07\par  Korean won   1179.10      1185.80         +0.57\par  Baht           41.83        43.08         +2.99\par  Peso           54.84        53.38         -2.66\par  Rupiah       8530.00      8940.00         +4.81.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030811dz8b00i27\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
