\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Pulled higher by rallying yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 748 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2003\par 11:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 8 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mostly\par strengthened on Friday as the Japanese yen's sharp rise against\par the U.S. dollar sent players scrambling to cover their short\par positions in regional plays.\par     The yen        rallied as high as 118.75 per dollar in\par offshore trade on Thursday tas it posted its biggest one day\par rise since March. The yen held around 119 yen on Friday,\par helping Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  shake off some of their shock from\par Tuesday's hotel bombing in Jakarta.\par  \par     "There is a broad U.S. dollar uncertainty back in the\par market," said Philip Wee, strategist at Singapore's DBS Bank.\par     "We don't expect any big \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves, but Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  general should benefit on the margin from the dollar \par \par \uc2  uncertainty amid the debate over how the bond-to-equity \par \par \uc2  migration would affect the dollar." \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah  rose nearly half a percent to \par \par \uc2  8,545 per dollar, before pulling back slightly. Earlier this \par \par \uc2  week it had tumbled to near three-month lows on the weaker side \par \par \uc2  of 8,700 per dollar after the bomb attack. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar , one of the region's most \par \par \uc2  liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plays, strengthened to 1.7533 per U.S dollar, \par \par \uc2  its highest since late July. It had fallen to a three-month low \par \par \uc2  of 1.7668 after the Jakarta bomb attack. \par \par \uc2  Even the Philippine peso , dogged by worries of \par \par \uc2  political instability since a failed mutiny on July 27, managed \par \par \uc2  some gains. But it ran into selling from local corporates and \par \par \uc2  ended local trade a touch softer at 54.71 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Wee said apart from the initial response to the bombing, \par \par \uc2  the rupiah's retracement from its lows had been in line with \par \par \uc2  recent moves in other high yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He said that showed that despite the talk of political and \par \par \uc2  economic woes, the rupiah would track the global dollar debate \par \par \uc2  as much as any other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We are placing our bets with the BI (Bank Indonesia), who \par \par \uc2  desires a 8200-8600 range for dollar/rupiah. It would be the \par \par \uc2  same in Philippines where we don't see the peso breaking \par \par \uc2  through \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's defence at 55 (per dollar)," he added. \par \par \uc2  While central banks in Philippines and Indonesia have been \par \par \uc2  spotted supporting their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , authorities in South \par \par \uc2  Korea, Taiwan and Thailand have been capping any significant \par \par \uc2  rise. \par \par \uc2  WON RISE CUT SHORT \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen's rise helped push the Korean won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to its strongest since Monday, with equity-related foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows helping the gains. Still, the fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the won's upside limited to 1,180.8 per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar  rose to a four-session high of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 34.401 per U.S. dollar before worries about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tempered those gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  advanced to 41.87 per dollar, from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late Thursday's 41.93, aided by moves in the Sing dollar and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A strong domestic economy and sustained foreign equity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows have boosted the baht in recent months, but the gains\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par have been capped by repeated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (BOT) Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Thursday there was no need for the bank to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its recent easing of some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  restrictions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the comments were unlikely to alleviate market wariness over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's tight \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  management.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It seems likely that the BOT will remain active in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market until other central banks in the region begin to step\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par aside from buying dollars to keep their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weak."\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0838 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.87       120.13         +1.06\par  Sing dlr      1.7548       1.7582         +0.19\par  Taiwan dlr    34.415       34.446         +0.09\par  Korean won   1181.10      1184.00         +0.24\par  Baht           41.88        41.93         +0.13\par  Peso           54.71        54.68         -0.05\par  Rupiah       8565.00      8587.00         +0.26\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.87       118.74         -0.11\par  Sing dlr      1.7548       1.7341         -1.18\par  Taiwan dlr    34.415       34.753         +0.99\par  Korean won   1181.10      1185.80         +0.42\par  Baht           41.88        43.08         +2.88\par  Peso           54.71        53.38         -2.43\par  Rupiah       8565.00      8940.00         +4.38.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030808dz8800i2c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
