\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Down vs dlr, outperform yen, euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 746 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 2003\par 05:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, July 16 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened\par against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday as investors scrambled out\par of short dollar positions after U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman\par Alan Greenspan sounded upbeat on the U.S. economic outlook.\par     But regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  outperformed the yen        and\par euro  against a strengthening dollar on expectations that\par a U.S. upturn would benefit Asia's exporters.\par     The Singapore dollar gapped down to a two-week trough of\par 1.7630 per U.S. dollar and the South Korean won\par   fell from five-month high to a one-week low of 1,183\par per dollar.\par     The Thai baht        fell to 41.67 per dollar, its lowest\par this week, after Tuesday's test of 41.50, where \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par has been suspected recently.\par     The dollar rose after Greenspan said the economy "could\par very well be embarking on a period of extended growth." His\par comments were good news for export-driven Asian economies, for\par whom U.S. is the single largest market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Today's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves back the view that Asia will\par outperform yen and euro whenever recovery in the U.S. picks\par up," said a dealer at a local bank.\par     The Singapore rose to test one-week highs of 67.45 yen\par   at 1.4824 Sing, about one yen off Tuesday's 11-month\par low, and it hit a two-month high of 1.9575 per euro .\par     The Korean won touched a five-month high of 9.9174 against\par the yen  and a three-month high of 1,308.82 against\par the euro .\par     However, Bhanu Baweja \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS said the\par move in the crosses was more based on capital flows rather than\par economic fundamentals.\par     "Its basically because U.S. bonds have been hit so much\par that all the short positions taken against the dollar taken on\par the basis of yield differential with yen and euro have been\par closed out," he said.\par     "The Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the other hand never saw that kind\par of flow in their fixed income assets, the broad theme still\par remains the equity flows and they remain quite positive."\par     Baweja said the fundamental view on Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par turn bullish only when evidence of a big rise in U.S. capital\par spending emerges, which would ensure higher Asian exports.\par     BAHT WATCHES BOT\par     The Thai baht, which has been a big recipient of foreign\par inflows this year, weakened as some foreign funds were spotted\par covering their short dollar positions, dealers in Singapore\par said.\par     They said the market was also wary of talk that a foreign\par bank was buying dollars on behalf of Thai authorities late on\par Tuesday, when the baht was testing 41.50 per dollar.\par     Dealers said the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent\par weeks around 41.50 to cap baht's strength that has been driven\par by the foreign investments in local stocks.\par     James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase in\par Singapore, said in a note that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had capped the\par baht by buying dollars at around the 41.52-41.55 range.\par     "We expect the BOT to continue to offset much of the equity\par flows," he said, but added that improved global and local\par growth prospects would eventually push the baht higher.\par     The Philippine peso        fell to a two-week low of 53.65\par per dollar, with corporates buying dollars to cover their\par requirements ahead of the import season that usually starts in\par early August and peaks in late September.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        also hit a two-week low of\par 8,248, with mainly Singapore-based funds spotted buying\par dollars.\par  \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0309 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.25       117.57         -0.58\par  Sing dlr      1.7613       1.7553         -0.34\par  Taiwan dlr    34.390       34.364         -0.08\par  Korean won   1177.50      1176.00         -0.13\par  Baht           41.63        41.52         -0.26\par  Peso           53.56        53.59         +0.05\par  Rupiah       8238.00      8222.00         -0.19\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.25       118.74         +0.41\par  Sing dlr      1.7613       1.7341         -1.54\par  Taiwan dlr    34.390       34.753         +1.06\par  Korean won   1177.50      1185.80         +0.70\par  Baht           41.63        43.08         +3.48\par  Peso           53.56        53.38         -0.34\par  Rupiah       8238.00      8940.00         +8.52.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030716dz7g007eq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
