\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won at 5-month high, rest eye Greenspan. \b0\par\par\uc2 752 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2003\par 10:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, July 15 (Reuters) - The South Korean won touched\par a five-month peak on Tuesday, while other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held\par on to their recent narrow ranges amid caution ahead of Federal\par Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's testimony later in the day.\par     The won                   rose to 1,174.6 per dollar, its\par strongest since February 5, before edging back to around 1,176\par level on wariness over authorities' sensitivity to a stronger\par won eroding export competitiveness.\par     The won has appreciated in recent weeks on a steady flow of\par foreign investment into local stocks, which clashes with an\par official bias for stimulative monetary conditions in an economy\par that is in recession.\par     The Bank of Korea (BOK) lowered its key call rate by 25\par basis point to a record low 3.75 percent last Thursday, and\par authorities have been spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to limit the won's\par gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Early Tuesday, a parliamentary committee approved a four\par trillion won increase in the limit on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par stabilisation fund bonds -- used to stem the won's strength.\par     Analysts said while the Bank of Korea will continue to curb\par any excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength, it might allow the won to\par strengthen against the U.S. dollar as long as it does not\par outperform the yen , a major trading partner and\par competitor.\par     "The market is cautious and no one can guess when\par authorities may choose to act, but as long as won is stable\par against the yen the chances of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are less," said\par Irene Cheung, ABN Amro's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist in Singapore.\par     The yen/won cross            was perched on the stronger\par side of the 10 won level, shy of Monday's high of 9.97 won\par where dealers in Singapore said state banks came in to pull the\par won down on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     SGD AWAITS GREENSPAN\par     The Singapore dollar        held on to a narrow\par 1.7550-1.7562 per U.S. dollar range, little moved by a\par surprisingly strong 10.9 percent seasonally adjusted monthly\par rise in May retail sales.\par     Thio Chin Loo, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at BNP Paribas said\par the market was holding back ahead of Greenspan's speech, which\par should provide fresh clues about the economic outlook.\par  \par     "Uninspiring. That's the mood of the markets right now with\par everything in suspense ahead of Greenspan's speech," she said.\par     She expected Greenspan to "play a balancing act" between\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par growth and inflation. And while he might emphasise the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prospects of an economic recovery, he also might want to calm\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par down the bond markets where longer dated yields have risen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sharply, she added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  fell to 41.60 per dollar, before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recovering towards 41.50 as local markets resumed trade after a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par long weekend. Dealers said with no major domestic data in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week, the baht was likely to track the Singapore dollar and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As well as cutting interest rates by 50 basis points in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late June, dealers have said the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around 41.50 in recent weeks to cap the baht, which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tested an 11-month high of 41.40 per dollar on three occasions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso  eased to around 53.635 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, its weakest level in local trade since June 27, as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporates sought dollars to cover their requirements ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the import season that usually starts in early August.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah  kept to the weak side of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 8,200 per dollar, but was clear of the two-week low of 8,235\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par set on Monday after a bomb exploded in the national\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par parliament.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0602 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.57       117.55         -0.02\par  Sing dlr      1.7553       1.7544         -0.05\par  Taiwan dlr    34.358       34.376         +0.05\par  Korean won   1176.00      1176.30         +0.03\par  Baht           41.52        41.50         -0.05\par  Peso           53.585       53.55         -0.07\par  Rupiah       8222.00      8225.00         +0.04\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.57       118.74         +1.00\par  Sing dlr      1.7553       1.7341         -1.21\par  Taiwan dlr    34.358       34.753         +1.15\par  Korean won   1176.00      1185.80         +0.83\par  Baht           41.52        43.08         +3.76\par  Peso           53.585       53.38         -0.38\par  Rupiah       8222.00      8940.00         +8.73.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030715dz7f00h4y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
