\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Contained, Sing waits on policy meet. \b0\par\par\uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2003\par 10:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, July 9 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were a mixed\par bag on Wednesday as traders speculated on policy changes in\par some markets, and the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  offset the\par appreciation pressure from inflows into the region's surging\par stock markets.\par     The Singapore dollar        bounced in a 1.7517-65 per\par dollar range ahead of Thursday's monetary policy review and\par second quarter growth data.\par     "There seems to be a split on whether the policy\par announcement will indicate a shift to an easing bias or not, so\par most players avoided taking any significant positions ahead of\par the event," a dealer at a local bank said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore does not set short-term\par interest rates, instead it targets the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in an\par undisclosed trade-weighted band to manage monetary conditions.\par     A poll by Reuters last week found most analysts expecting\par no change in the neutral policy stance of the MAS, while a\par minority saw an implicit shift to an easier bias.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers said Monday's data showing an $830 million rise\par in reserves in June, had reignited speculation the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par had been buying dollars to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weak and may\par formally announce a widening of the band on Thursday.\par     Bank of America calculated the rise at $1.13 billion, after\par adjusting for the euro's weakness. Still, it said risk of an\par explicit or implicit shift to loosening was 25 percent at most.\par     Thio Chin Loo, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at BNP Paribas,\par said Singapore authorities might have bought dollars to counter\par portfolio inflows, and maintained her view of no policy change.\par     "With the second quarter likely to have been the worst\par quarter of the year, it is unlikely the MAS will act behind the\par curve," she said.\par     Capital inflows, mainly in stocks, have increased across\par Asia, putting appreciation pressure on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -- something\par local central banks want to head off to keep exports\par competitive and monetary conditions easy.\par     Central banks in Thailand, the Philippines, Hong Kong and\par Taiwan have eased policy since the U.S. Federal Reserve cut\par rates by 25 basis points on June 25.\par     KOREAN POLICY MEET\par     South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also meets on Thursday, and\par authorities there have been trying to counter won\par   strength from a surge of equity-related inflows.\par     The won rose to 1,178.4 per dollar, against late Tuesday's\par 1,180.2, but fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was seen resisting its return\par to five-month highs of 1,176.2 hit on Monday.\par     The Taiwan dollar          was also up, helped by a stock\par market  around 12-month highs, but wary of Monday's\par 10-month intraday highs of 34.305 per U.S. dollar on aggressive\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     In \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , some offshore funds sold the baht        down\par to 41.71 per dollar. Dealers said the moves in major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par and fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities had prompted players to\par cut back on short U.S. dollar positions.\par  \par     The Indonesian rupiah        eased past 8,200 per dollar,\par after hitting a one-month high of 8,153 on Monday.\par     The Philippine peso        fell to 53.51 per dollar, its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lowest since June 30, but ended slightly higher on news that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par proceeds of the government's $750 million bond issue would be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lent to state-run National Power Corp, ending its commercial\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par requirements for the year.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0818 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.12       118.23         +0.09\par  Sing dlr      1.7544       1.7555         +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    34.337       34.380         +0.13\par  Korean won   1179.00      1180.20         +0.10\par  Baht           41.68        41.62         -0.14\par  Peso           53.43        53.44         +0.02\par  Rupiah       8195.00      8178.00         -0.21\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.12       118.74         +0.52\par  Sing dlr      1.7544       1.7341         -1.16\par  Taiwan dlr    34.337       34.753         +1.21\par  Korean won   1179.00      1185.80         +0.58\par  Baht           41.68        43.08         +3.36\par  Peso           53.43        53.38         -0.09\par  Rupiah       8195.00      8940.00