\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Step back, wary of central banks. \b0\par\par\uc2 740 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2003\par 11:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, July 8 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  faltered\par despite rallying stock markets on Tuesday, with most giving up\par ground to a U.S. dollar that, buoyed by gains on Wall Street,\par strengthened to two-month highs against the euro .\par     Dealers said the dollar's rise and worries about\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Asian central banks had raised doubts about\par sustainability of gains in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , including the\par yen , which briefly rose to two week highs around 117.60.\par     Asian stock markets, impressed by Wall Street's rally,\par posted more gains which would attract more foreign investment\par that should boost Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -- something local central\par banks want to head off so their exports stay competitive.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "We remain sceptical whether central banks in the region\par will be in a hurry to allow their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to appreciate in\par any significant manner, given their caution on prospects for\par global and regional economic recovery," said Sameer Goel,\par analyst at Bank of America in Singapore.\par     Central banks in Thailand, the Philippines, Hong Kong and\par Taiwan have eased policy since the U.S. Federal Reserve cut\par rates by 25 basis points on June 25. Monetary policy reviews\par are due in South Korea and Singapore on Thursday.\par     The Singapore dollar        eased towards 1.7580 per U.S.\par dollar to be down about one-third of a percent on Tuesday as\par the market remained anxious ahead of Thursday's policy review\par by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore.\par     Dealers said thin volumes ahead of the review could make\par price action in the Singapore dollar volatile. The MAS manages\par the dollar, its main policy tool, against a trade-weighted\par basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of major trade partners and competitors.\par     A poll by Reuters last week found most analysts expecting\par no change in the neutral policy stance of the MAS, while a\par minority saw an implicit shift to an easier bias.\par     The South Korean won                   posted gains as the\par Korean stock market  ended at a seven-month high, but it\par avoided Monday's five-month highs which had prompted\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that dealers estimated at about $1 billion.\par     Dealers said state banks were active again late on Tuesday.\par     The Taiwan dollar          was also up, helped by a stock\par market  at 12-month highs, but wary of Monday's 10-month\par highs after dealers spotted aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  just before Monday's close. Traders said the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was active on Tuesday as well.\par     BOT SAYS OUT OF MARKET\par     Comments from the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that it did not need to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the baht after last month's 50 basis point rate\par cut had little impact on the market, as dealers in Bangkok\par still expected rallies to be capped by authorities.\par     "After the rate cut, we've seen slower capital inflows and\par the baht has been stable, so there's no need for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to look after it for now," Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula\par said.\par     But dealers said the moves in major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and fear of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities to cap baht strength had prompted\par players to cut back on short U.S. dollar positions.\par  \par     "They (the BOT) bought quite a large amount of dollars only\par last Friday," said a dealer.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        eased back the 8,200 per\par dollar level, after a hitting a one-month high of 8,153 on\par Monday.\par     The Philippine peso        held on to a narrow 53.36-53.43\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range, and has held a narrow 53.23/44 range in the week since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  delivered a surprise interest rate cut.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0804 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.23       117.99         -0.20\par  Sing dlr      1.7555       1.7498         -0.32\par  Taiwan dlr    34.356       34.405         +0.14\par  Korean won   1180.10      1181.90         +0.15\par  Baht           41.62        41.59         -0.07\par  Peso           53.44        53.35         -0.16\par  Rupiah       8178.00      8167.00         -0.13\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.23       118.74         +0.43\par  Sing dlr      1.7555       1.7341         -1.22\par  Taiwan dlr   