\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Thai PM Thaksin sees baht strengthening. \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2003\par 08:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 3 (Reuters) - Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said on Thursday he expected the baht would tend to strengthen in the future, due to continuing capital inflows that have helped push Thai shares to three-year highs. \par \par \uc2  "Investors see very bright prospects and investment potential. The baht has been very stable and tends to strengthen rather than weaken," Thaksin told reporters when asked why the Thai stock market was rising so rapidly. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Stock Exchange of Thailand composite index has gained over 34 percent so far this year to hit 492.95 - its highest level since January 2000. At 0600 GMT, the SET index was up two percent at 487.41. \par \par \uc2  The baht has gained almost three percent since the end of last year and gained further following Thaksin's comments to trade around 41.765 to the dollar, its strongest level this week. \par \par \uc2  "The baht has strengthened following the PM's comment, but I don't think we should read too much into it because he was only commenting on the stock market performance," Simon Flint, Bank of America \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week cut its key interest rate by 50 basis points to 1.25 percent in a move that analysts said was designed to cap baht gains and keep exports competitive following a cut in U.S. interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Bangkok said most players in the market were still wary of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sensitivity to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength. \par \par \uc2  "Thaksin's statements are mostly taken by the market as political. It's the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that sets the tone in the market," said a dealer at a local bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month as the baht touched 11-month highs of 41.40 per dollar. (With additional reporting by Ovais Subhani in Singapore). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030703dz7300c1d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
