\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Up Slightly On 6th Anniversary Of Float \b0\par\par\uc2 732 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2003\par 12:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht ended slightly stronger against the dollar in Asian trade Wednesday, the sixth anniversary of the float of the baht in the midst of the financial crisis of 1997, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The baht's rise was due to general weakness in the U.S. unit versus regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was believed to have stepped in to cap the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains, they said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 41.925 baht, down from THB41.95 late in offshore trade Tuesday and a close of THB42.085 Monday. Thai markets were closed Tuesday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said exporters capped the dollar's intraday high at THB42.00, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held the bottom around THB41.90. \par \par \uc2  "It looks like the big guy doesn't want to let it slide," a trader at a foreign bank said, in a reference to suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by agents of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Wednesday that last week's 50-basis-point cut in the official 14-day repurchase market target rate to 1.25% had succeeded in slowing speculative short-term capital inflows, but that it would take another month or two to see the full effects. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it wants to restrain any excessive appreciation in the baht, so that volatility is muted and the country's exports remain competitive. \par \par \uc2  If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market Wednesday, it was in a much better position than it was six years ago, when it was forced to concede that it had wasted its foreign reserves in a failed defense of a fixed exchange rate mechanism which had previously kept the dollar around THB25. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's foreign reserves stood at a high $39.4 billion as of June 20, and any dollar buying Wednesday would have only boosted the figure. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar-baht exchange rate has been relatively stable for the past three years in a range of THB40 to THB46. \par \par \uc2  Most economists have projected that the dollar will continue to weaken gradually against the baht in the second half of 2003, due to a general decline expected in the dollar versus regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and to inflows attracted by the relative strength of the Thai economy. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to restrain the baht's appreciation and secondarily to further strengthen foreign reserves. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was expected to open Thursday in Asia in a range of THB41.85 to THB42.00. \par \par \uc2  Prices of most Thai government bond extended their rally Wednesday as yields continued to fall in adjustment to last Friday's 14-day policy rate cut, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Siam Commercial Bank's announcement earlier Wednesday of a 25 to 50 basis point cut in its deposit and lending rates, effective Thursday, also boosted sentiment, they added. \par \par \uc2  Siam Commercial's savings rate will fall to a new historic low of 0.75%, an easing that other commercial banks are expected to soon follow to avoid unwanted deposits. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the short-term government bond due December 2006 finished in a bid-offer range of 1.39%-1.37%, down from Monday's close of 1.41%. \par \par \uc2  The long-term bond due November 2012 finished at 2.22%-2.20% versus 2.25% previous close. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected short- and medium-term yields to remain under pressure for the rest of the week because of high liquidity in the financial system \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand auctioned Wednesday THB1.5 billion of November 2022 bonds at an average yield of 3.5745%, slightly higher than what the market expected. However, the result had no impact on the secondary market as the issue was illiquid. \par \par \uc2  The overnight interbank rate settled at a new range of 1.125%-1.25% in line with the lower 14-day target rate. The 1-day repo rate had already fallen since Friday afternoon to an appropriate range capped by the 14-day rate. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market     Term            Wednesday       Monday\par Interbank  Overnight/Late  1.125%-1.2500%  1.25000%\par Repurchase Overnight/Close 1.12500%        1.12500%\par            14-Day          1.25000%        1.25000%\par            1-Month         1.25000%        1.28125%\par            3-Month         no activity     no activity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Thomas Fox and Suttinee Yuvejwattana, Dow Jones Newswires;\par 662-266-0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030702dz72000o8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
