\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Slightly Higher In Thin, Pre-FOMC Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 655 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 2003\par 12:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht closed marginally higher against the dollar Monday after marking time for most of the day, thanks to late gains in the yen. \par \par \uc2  Trading was very thin as most investors sat on the sidelines ahead of the U.S. Federal Open Market Commitee's two-day meeting, starting Tuesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 41.57 baht, down a tad from THB41.60 at the Asian close Friday. \par \par \uc2  After languishing in a narrow THB41.59 to THB41.61 band for most of the local session, the dollar dropped marginally in late trade to its day's low of THB41.56 as it declined slightly against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "The market is very ... very thin. It seems like nobody wants to trade. I think they are waiting for the Fed's verdict," said a local bank trader. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said there's no need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market now as the baht's level is satisfactory. \par \par \uc2  He said equity-related inflows had strengthened the baht significantly, although such inflows have subsided. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors were buying large amounts of Thai shares last week, but by the end of the week, the upward momentum had dissipated more or less. Foreigners were net buyers of THB176.1 million worth of Thai shares Friday, down from THB1.53 billion Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is expected to move in a range of THB41.50 to THB41.65 Tuesday. Trade will likely remain thin until the FOMC meeting concludes. \par \par \uc2  Prices of long-term Thai government bonds ended lower Monday in thin trade on profit-taking in most issues, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Trading was quite thin, which magnified the yields' rise. Many investors were on the sidelines, looking forward to the Fed's decision on the rate cut and the July schedule for government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond auctions," said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Yields of most long-term government bonds were up around four-to-six basis points from Friday's closing levels. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Open Market Committee is expected to cut U.S. interest rates by 25 or 50 basis points this week. A 50-basis-point cut could lead to a faster recovery in ground given up by Thai bonds in recent profit-taking. \par \par \uc2  "Many investors unwound positions, waiting for good timing to build up their portfolio after the Fed's announcement," said another dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  The government bond maturing June 2009 ended at 2.01% compared with 1.965% at Friday's close, the Thai Bond Dealing Center said in its daily report. The April 2010 issue finished at 2.11%, up from the previous close of 2.08%, and the November 2012 issue closed at 2.525%, up from 2.4815%. \par \par \uc2  Yields of short- and medium-term goverment bonds were up only about zero-to-two basis points, however, due to demand driven by high financial system liquidity. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold at an auction Monday THB1 billion worth of 91-day treasury bills at an average yield of 1.3836%, down from 1.40% last week. \par \par \uc2  The auction result came in below the secondary market yield curve, as expected, due to heavy demand for big lots of short-term securities to help big banks cover the costs of excess deposits. \par \par \uc2  Overnight interbank rates remained in a tight range with support from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowing through the repurchase market to absorb excess liquidity in the system, dealers said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market     Term            Monday            Friday\par Interbank  Overnight/Late  1.65%-1.6875%     1.65%-1.6875%\par Repurchase Overnight/Close 1.65625%          1.65625%\par            14-Day          1.75000%          1.75000%\par            1-Month         no activity       no activity\par            3-Month         no activity       no activity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana and Supunnabul Suwannakij, Dow Jones\par Newswires; 662 266 0744; djn.bangkok@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Edited by Ryan Woo\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030623dz6n000nx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
