\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dlr slips, others wait for FOMC. \b0\par\par\uc2 717 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 2003\par 11:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, June 23 (Reuters) - An afternoon slip in the\par Singapore dollar livened up otherwise lethargic Asian trading\par on Monday, as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were mostly content to sit pat as they\par waited for an expected U.S. interest rate cut later in the\par week.\par     The U.S. dollar has found interest ahead of Wednesday's\par expected rate cut on forecasts of a second-half upturn and\par further gains in rallying equity markets, although the yen did\par post some late gains.\par     But Asia's stock markets have also been gaining strongly,\par and the investment flows have supported regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par despite the efforts of some central banks to limit their gains\par and preserve export competitiveness.\par  \par     A pause in the regional equity market upturn, apart from\par Thailand, helped the subdued tone of most \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday.\par     "Basically, I'm surprised it lasted this long. This\par tapering off of the stock markets in Asia did not surprise me\par at all," a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader in Singapore said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar        was pushed to a one-week low\par just shy of 1.74 per U.S. dollar after a large sell order and\par some disappointing inflation data, dealers said.\par     The CPI fell an adjusted 0.7 percent in May from April, and\par fell 0.1 percent from a year earlier, both weaker than\par expected.\par     Weekend comments from Deputy Prime Minister and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  head Lee Hsien Loong that the Singapore economy would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rebound in the second half of 2003 helped scale back\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectations of a monetary easing at a July policy review,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Global markets are certain that the Federal Reserve will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cut rates at the end of its meeting on Wednesday. The only\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par question is whether that cut will be 25 or 50 basis points.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In a report, Bank of America said a 25 basis point cut\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would be a disappointment and could see some gains in Southeast\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the dollar, while 50 basis points\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par might focus attention on the high-yielding Philippine peso\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   and Indonesian rupiah       .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Likewise, a relatively aggressive Fed would conjure\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par optimism about an early recovery in Asia, and perhaps inspire\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par those who would seek to be long Singapore dollars, as we are at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par present, and inspire confidence in the Thai baht, which is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par enjoying a generous welter of portfolio inflows," BOA said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "On the latter, we think that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hold the line and the Singapore dollar has more space to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appreciate than the baht."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NO NEED TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Monday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the baht  had been stable - it held above 41.55 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar on Monday - and he saw no need for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The baht exchange rate is okay and there's no need to do\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par anything. It can be left to move by itself and it has been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stable," the governor said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders have reported the BOT has been an active buyer of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars this month, and the baht seems wary of pushing through\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 41.50 per dollar. The baht has stalled at 41.40 - a high since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par last July - on three occasions in June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine government denied local newspaper reports it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was planning a $500 million global bond to fund its budget\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deficit, but the peso still softened on the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Exporters in Korea and Taiwan were dollar sellers, helping\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par both the Korean won             and Taiwan dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   end largely unchanged.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0812 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.90       118.32         +0.36\par  Sing dlr      1.7387       1.7354         -0.19\par  Taiwan dlr    34.591       34.587         -0.01\par  Korean won   1190.20      1190.50         +0.03\par  Baht           41.54        41.58         +0.10\par  Peso           53.40        53.30         -0.19\par  Rupiah       8245.00      8237.00         -0.10\par     Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.90       118.74         +0.71\par  Sing dlr      1.7387       1.7341         -0.26\par  Taiwan dlr    34.591       34.753         +0.47\par  Korean won   1190.20      1185.80         -0.37\par  Baht           41.54        43.08         +3.71\par  Peso           53.40        53.38         -0.04\par  Rupiah       8245.00      8940.00         +8.43.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030623dz6n00ij0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
