\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Flat; Off Low On Late Onshore Dlr Selling \b0\par\par\uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2003\par 13:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht ended flat Wednesday after the dollar gave up early gains due to onshore selling once the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came off highs against other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 41.79 baht, unchanged from the Asian close Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged to an intraday high of THB41.89 in early morning trade due mainly to demand from European banks in Bangkok, traders said. Dollar buying was also strong due to caution that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  Dealers suspected agents of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were buying dollars Tuesday around THB41.70 when the U.S. unit quickly jumped above THB41.80. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's gains Wednesday gradually ebbed away as local banks sold the U.S. unit in the afternoon as it slipped against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially the yen, the regional trendsetter. The dollar touched an intraday low of THB41.77 in the afternoon. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula told reporters Wednesday he couldn't confirm whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been active in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Late last month, Pridiyathorn confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought dollars to slow the baht's appreciation so it would stay competitive with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Thailand's trading partners. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asia, the U.S. unit was quoted at Y117.72, compared with its early high of Y118.13. \par \par \uc2  Traders expected the U.S. unit to move within a THB41.75-THB41.90 range Thursday morning, subject to volatility in the yen. \par \par \uc2  Thai government bond prices ended sharply higher Wednesday, pushing yields on most issues to fresh historic lows, thanks to an overnight rally in U.S. Treasurys. Siam Commercial Bank's decision to cut its key interest rates across the board Wednesday also gave bonds a boost, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Bond yields dropped from the open as investors took cues from U.S. Treasurys and then fell further on news of Siam Commercial Bank's rate cut. \par \par \uc2  Siam, the country's fourth-largest commercial bank, will cut its deposit rates by between 25 and 50 basis points and key lending rates by 25 basis points, effective Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The cut is the first by a large Thai bank in what appears to be a new round of interest rate cuts driven by flush liquidity in the system, and signs of lower global interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The most active government bond due December 2006 closed Wednesday at 1.65%, down from 1.67% the previous day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The November 2011 bond finished at 2.24%, down from a close Wednesday of 2.34%, while the November 2012 bond dropped to 2.42% versus 2.52% at the last close. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said yields will likely hover around current levels for some time, while the market waits to see if the U.S. and Thai authorities will cut rates. \par \par \uc2  "Profit-taking can't push yields up as demand from long-term investors is still strong. The low supply and low interest rate trend still provide a firm buffer for any upside (for yields)," said a foreign bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand sold THB1 billion of a reopened November 2022 bond Wednesday at 3.6279%, down from 3.65% at the closing level Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Overnight interbank rates were flat, despite flush liquidity in the financial system, due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's firm support for its 14-day target rate. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market     Term            Wednesday         Tuesday\par Interbank  Overnight/Late  1.6875%           1.6875%\par Repurchase Overnight/Close 1.65625%          1.65625%\par            14-Day          1.75000%          1.75000%\par            1-Month         no activity       no activity\par            3-Month         no activity       no activity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Ratthapol Onsanit and Suttinee Yuvejwattana, Dow Jones Newswires;\par 662 266 0744; djn.bangkok@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Edited by Simon Harvey\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030611dz6b000ru\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
