\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Weighed on by stocks despite weak dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2003\par 10:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, June 10 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held an\par easier tone on Tuesday despite a weaker U.S. dollar, with the\par Singapore dollar and Thai baht hitting fresh one-week lows and\par the Korean won posting a new two-week high before pulling back.\par     They were hesitant after U.S. stocks eased and the dollar\par fell when an accounting scandal rocked America's second-largest\par mortgage finance company, Freddie Mac (FRE.N).\par     Those worries hit Asian stocks and analysts said if the\par recent equity rally were to pause, the foreign investment flows\par that had buoyed regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could ease as well.\par     "People are watching stock market moves, particularly\par developments in the U.S. regarding Freddie Mac," said Thio Chin\par Loo, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at BNP Paribas in Singapore.\par  \par     "With the stocks front looking a bit more dicey, investors\par seem to be keen to take some chips off the table," she added.\par     Still, foreign equity investors were net buyers of South\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korean stocks and powered the won             to a two\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week high, before fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  capped its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The won ended local trade at 1,194.5 per dollar, off an\par early high of 1,192.2 which was its strongest since May 26.\par     The Singapore dollar rose to 1.7245 per U.S. dollar, before\par it wiped those gains and fell back to around 1.7332.\par     Dealers said growing speculation about what would be in a\par mid-year policy review by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore,\par due in July, had added to the selling pressure.\par     The focus on Singapore's monetary policy has increased as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par central banks in the region and around the world cut rates and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after the Singapore government said it expects the economy to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shrink in the second quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The MAS manages the exchange rate, its main monetary policy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tool, against an undisclosed basket of trade-weighted\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  eased to 41.78 per dollar, off 41.60\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in early trade. Dealers in Bangkok said dollar bids around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 41.60, suspected to be on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exaggerated its fall.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last Friday had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to pull the\par baht down from a 10-month high of 41.41 per dollar.\par     Elsewhere, the Philippine peso        recovered from\par two-month lows and the Indonesian rupiah  held a tight\par range just below the 8,200 per dollar level.\par     Dealers in Jakarta said rupiah was under some pressure on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar demand from local corporates. But it was underpinned by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hopes of rising dollar inflows from government asset sales.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0806 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.15       118.39         +0.20\par  Sing dlr      1.7318       1.7283         -0.20\par  Taiwan dlr    34.675       34.662         -0.04\par  Korean won   1194.20      1196.70         +0.21\par  Baht           41.75        41.68         -0.17\par  Peso           53.37        53.38         +0.03\par  Rupiah       8195.00      8180.00         -0.18\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.15       118.74         +0.50\par  Sing dlr      1.7318       1.7341         +0.13\par  Taiwan dlr    34.675       34.753         +0.22\par  Korean won   1194.20      1185.80         -0.70\par  Baht           41.75        43.08         +3.19\par  Peso           53.37        53.38         +0.03\par  Rupiah       8195.00      8940.00         +9.09.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030610dz6a00hao\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
