\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Drift lower on yen, c.bank fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 758 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2003\par 06:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, June 9 (Reuters) - A bounce in the U.S. dollar\par extended the retreat of Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from recent highs\par early on Monday, with the Singapore dollar, Thai baht and\par Taiwan dollar falling to their lowest in about a week.\par     The Philippine peso        fell to a two-month low on\par expectations of more monetary easing after last week's\par restoration of a system of decreasing interest rates for larger\par bank deposits at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Indonesian rupiah        was slightly softer around\par 8,200 per dollar, with the market showing little response to\par the sale of a controlling stake in Bank Danamon's (BDMN.JK) to\par Singapore's Temasek Holdings. For details click             .\par     Dealers in Jakarta said with the widely expected deal set\par to be completed on June 16, the market would wait and see what\par dollar component of the sale hits the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The deal was\par estimated to be worth over $350 million, but some of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions may have been completed, dealers\par said.\par     More broadly, the U.S. dollar's rise against the yen\par and euro , and resistance by some regional central banks\par to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength, has prompted investors to adjust their\par positions in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers and analysts said .\par  \par     "Asia is trading lower mainly on the dollar/yen move," said\par Craig Chan, analyst at Forecast Ltd in Singapore.\par     "There shouldn't be any surprise on central banks' easier\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bias after the weak second quarter numbers we had seen so far,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par he added referring to the impact of the SARS outbreak on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exports and growth in the region.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PESO SETS FRESH 2-MONTH LOW\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso  had its own reasons to fall to 53.57 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, its weakest since March 31. It pared some of those\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par losses but dealers in Manila said the bias was still for more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The market is looking at more policy easing to come," said\par chief dealer of a local bank in Manila.\par     Last week's restoration of the tiering system was seen as a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par de facto easing as it would boost liquidity. The tiered system\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was scrapped for a flat rate in March, when the peso was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par threatening record lows and money supply was rising.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "And despite some good news over deficit, there is some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par scepticism about how well the fiscal situation really is," he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said, referring to May tax collections being above target.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, the Thai baht  slipped to an early 41.75\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar. It recovered a little, but was still well clear of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 10-month high of 41.41 hit on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht ran into selling on Friday after the Bank of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap its rise and Governor Pridiyathorn\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Devakula said he expected the baht to soften at some point.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Chan said foreign portfolio investments and relatively\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par better economic growth prospects should keep the baht\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par supported.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bias would have an impact in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short-term. But on a medium term basis baht will be one of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outperformers in the region," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thailand's resistance to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains also hit sentiment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the Singapore dollar , which drifted further away from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent two-week highs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Sing dollar was around the 1.7300 per U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level, against last week's high of 1.7162, its strongest since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par May 15.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and monetary easing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around the region was making investors in Singapore dollar a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bit worried ahead of the island's scheduled policy announcement\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par early July.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore manages exchange rate, its main monetary policy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tool, against an undisclosed basket of trade-weighted\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of its major trading partners. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DOLLAR AT 0330 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change 