\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Ease as U.S. dollar slide pauses. \b0\par\par\uc2 676 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2003\par 11:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, May 28 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eased on\par Wednesday as a pause in the U.S. dollar's decline against the\par euro and yen prompted investors to consolidate their positions\par in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Thai baht        held off Tuesday's 10-month highs,\par helped by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  saying it had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recently to\par stop the baht rising too fast, and the Indonesian rupiah\par drifted further away from the near three-year highs it hit on\par Monday.\par     The Singapore dollar        and Korean won\par   touched their lowest levels in about a week, and the\par Taiwan dollar  touched a two-week trough.\par     The Philippine peso        was at a one-month low when the\par local market was closed an hour early due to a tropical storm\par that has caused widespread flooding in the capital.\par     Analysts said most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which have lost ground\par in trade-weighted terms despite gains against the dollar, still\par had room to appreciate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Given the market was long of dollars,\par some profit-taking was not surprising.\par     "The new mantra for most Asians is likely to be weakness on\par a trade weighted basis; this may mean some strength against the\par dollar," said Sameer Goel of Bank of America in Singapore.\par     He added that stability against the dollar was also\par important given most trade and foreign debt is denominated in\par dollars, and often not hedged due to a lack of depth in local\par markets.\par     "Strength against the dollar does improve balance sheets,\par while trade-weighted weakness protects export competitiveness.\par This combination is possibly a good defence in a world of large\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves," he said.\par     CENTRAL BANKS ACTIVE\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (BOT) said it had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par recently to stop the baht from strengthening too fast.\par     "We had a lot of capital inflows recently and so we had to\par manage the baht to prevent it from becoming too strong\par unnaturally," governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said.\par  \par     The baht eased as far as 41.78 per dollar from an offshore\par high of 41.55, which was its strongest since July 2002.\par     At its high, the baht was 3.7 percent above its April 25\par lows, driven by robust growth and capital inflows. The stock\par market hit an 11-month high on Wednesday.\par     Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Burhanuddin Abdullah said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the rupiah was not overvalued despite gains of over eight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent against the dollar this year, driven by improving\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic indicators and investors seeking high-yield assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Tracking moves in dollar/yen, the Singapore dollar fell to\par around 1.7290 per U.S. dollar, its lowest since May 20.\par     Dealers said the Sing could see further losses, but some\par major players were spotted supporting it at 1.7280-1.7290.\par     The South Korean won                   ended local trade at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a one-week low, pressured by a widening current account deficit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the Finance Ministry's plans to sell one trillion won of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stabilisation fund bonds next week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said the bond sale would suck dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par liquidity, flowing from exporters and foreign portfolio\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors, out of the market and limit demand for the won -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par effectively a form of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap won strength.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0840 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.60       116.79         -0.69\par  Sing dlr      1.7268       1.7216         -0.30\par  Taiwan dlr    34.721       34.712         -0.03\par  Korean won   1200.40      1198.60         -0.15\par  Baht           41.68        41.68          0.00\par  Peso           53.10        52.88         -0.41\par  Rupiah       8215.00      8175.00         -0.49\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.60       118.74         +0.97\par  Sing dlr      1.7268       1.7341         +0.42\par  Taiwan dlr    34.721       34.753         +0.09\par  Korean won   1200.40      1185.80         -1.22\par  Baht           41.68        43.08         +3.36\par  Peso           53.10        53.38         +0.53\par  Rupiah       8215.00      8940.00         +8.83.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030528dz5s00jgg\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\b